{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCJekaiRDoPVjUdsp2j5wh","type":"tool_result","content":"1280\t  itself, limping. A second topple, from the remaining knees, breaks the cockpit open and Krake ejects.\n1281\t\n1282\t**ADMIRAL KRAKE** (3-B, phase 2, 90 s; 40 HP):\n1283\t- He rolls and dashes between the control-room consoles.\n1284\t- He fires **flares** with both pistols: slow, glowing, shootable, bursting into firework sparks.\n1285\t- He throws smoke, which cuts visibility to 40% for 3 s.\n1286\t- He summons 2 Red Tide at a time.\n1287\t- **FINAL SHOT.** At 15% HP he lunges for the master sluice lever. Slow motion (presentation timeScale 0.3) and a\n1288\t  3-second ring show over the lever arm; hitting the arm or the lever wins. A miss means he pulls it partway: the water\n1289\t  surges, \"TIDE RISING!\", and the fight resumes; repeat until it lands.\n1290\t- **Defeat**: \"The sea… always… wins…\" Kai: \"Not today.\" Then the ending.\n1291\t\n1292\t**Mini-bosses**: **BULLDOG** (1-3), **THE GULL** (2-3) and **SEAWOLF** (3-2 and 3-4) are registered as bosses with an\n1293\tHP bar but no intro card.\n1294\t\n1295\t### 5.8 Training: the CREST RANGE (Juno instructs)\n1296\tAn indoor range of concrete lanes with dividers, plywood cut-outs of Black Current goons on rails, and score lamps.\n1297\t1. **AIM & FIRE**: 6 pop-up cut-outs at 8–15 m. \"AIM [stick/mouse] · FIRE [R2/Left click]\".\n1298\t2. **COVER & RELOAD**: a turret robot (a box with a red lamp) telegraphs 3 shots; hide for each. Then empty the\n1299\t   magazine and reload in cover. \"HOLD [L2] TO TAKE COVER — YOU RELOAD IN COVER\".\n1300\t3. **WEAPONS**: shoot an orange-vest cut-out for MG ammo, switch with [R1], shred 3 drone targets; a shotgun on a\n1301\t   shield cut-out; the GL on a crate stack. \"[R1]/[L1] — OR FIRE WHILE IN COVER — TO SWITCH\".\n1302\t4. **READ THE CRISIS**: a Red Tide cut-out (a fast telegraph), a grenade lob (shoot it), a civilian cut-out (\"DON'T\n1303\t   SHOOT\"), then a timed drill: 8 targets in 20 s, with the TIME HUD.\n1304\t\n1305\t\"TRAINING COMPLETE\" records the best time. The first ARCADE start offers Training once (and `seenTraining` remembers).\n1306\t\n1307\t### 5.9 Script (every story beat; the lines are original)\n1308\t- **Briefing 1** (HQ):\n1309\t  - HALE: \"Agents. Two hours ago the Black Current seized Port Lumen's harbor and the Tidewall.\"\n1310\t  - HALE: \"Their leader is Silas Krake. A disgraced admiral with a grudge the size of an ocean.\"\n1311\t  - JUNO: \"He'll open the floodgates at dawn. King tide. The whole city goes under.\"\n1312\t  - HALE: \"You have until 06:00. Land at Lantern Pier. Find his signal. End this.\"\n1313\t  - KAI: \"Understood. CREST is on it.\"\n1314\t- **1-0 intro**:\n1315\t  - MARI: \"Hang on! Lumen Coast Guard express—next stop, trouble!\"\n1316\t  - KRAKE (screens): \"Citizens of Port Lumen! Enjoy your lanterns. They are the last lights you will see.\"\n1317\t  - KRAKE: \"At dawn the king tide comes, and I open every gate. The sea takes back what you stole!\"\n1318\t  - ROOK: \"Charming guy.\"\n1319\t  - KAI: \"Let's make some waves.\"\n1320\t  - ROOK: \"Kid, you say that every mission.\"\n1321\t- **1-1**:\n1322\t  - JUNO: \"Hostiles on the pier! Watch the festival crowd!\"\n1323\t  - JUNO, at the quartermaster: \"Orange vest! He's hauling ammo—drop him!\"\n1324\t  - KAI, on the clear: \"Pier's clear. Moving!\"\n1325\t- **1-2**:\n1326\t  - ROOK: \"Market hall. Stay sharp.\"\n1327\t  - JUNO: \"Red uniform! That's Red Tide—they don't miss. Hit him first!\"\n1328\t  - JUNO: \"Grenade! Shoot it out of the air!\"\n1329\t  - ROOK, when the gallery falls: \"Now that's what I call fresh fish.\"\n1330\t- **1-3**:\n1331\t  - JUNO: \"Something big is coming through the containers!\"\n1332\t  - KAI: \"Armored truck! Take out the gunner!\"\n1333\t  - ROOK: \"Fuel tank—light it up!\"\n1334\t  - WORKER: \"Don't shoot! I just work here!\"\n1335\t- **1-4**:\n1336\t  - MARI: \"Grab something! We're taking the canals!\"\n1337\t  - JUNO: \"Jet skis, three o'clock!\"\n1338\t  - MARI: \"Low bridge! Heads down!\"\n1339\t  - ROOK: \"Fireworks barge. Happy festival.\"\n1340\t- **1-B**:\n1341\t  - BARRACUDA: \"CREST! The Admiral said you'd come. He didn't say you'd be this slow!\"\n1342\t  - BARRACUDA: \"Say hello to the Stingray!\"\n1343\t  - BARRACUDA, phase 3: \"Enough! I'll do this myself!\"\n1344\t  - MARI: \"Torpedo in the water! Shoot it!\"\n1345\t  - BARRACUDA, on defeat: \"This isn't over, CREST!\"\n1346\t- **1-Z outro**:\n1347\t  - JUNO: \"Krake's signal is coming from Lighthouse Point.\"\n1348\t  - MARI: \"Gull's Rest. They've held my father there since yesterday.\"\n1349\t  - KAI: \"Then that's where we're going.\"\n1350\t  - ROOK: \"Into a storm. Naturally.\"\n1351\t- **Briefing 2**:\n1352\t  - HALE: \"The lighthouse relays Krake's commands to the whole fleet.\"\n1353\t  - JUNO: \"Take it out and his ships go deaf. Also, it's raining. A lot.\"\n1354\t- **2-0 intro**:\n1355\t  - KRAKE (intercept): \"Hammerhead. No one reaches the lamp.\"\n1356\t  - HAMMERHEAD: \"NOBODY. PASSES. HAMMERHEAD.\"\n1357\t  - ROOK: \"He talks in capital letters.\"\n1358\t- **2-1**:\n1359\t  - JUNO: \"Blades! Don't let them get close!\"\n1360\t  - KAI: \"Shotgun. Now we're talking.\"\n1361\t  - FISHERMAN: \"Not me! Not me!\"\n1362\t- **2-2**:\n1363\t  - JUNO: \"Shield! Knock it aside with the shotgun!\"\n1364\t  - ROOK: \"Ropes! They're coming through the roof!\"\n1365\t- **2-3**:\n1366\t  - MARI: \"The funicular's the only way up the cliff.\"\n1367\t  - JUNO: \"Car coming down—it's full of them!\"\n1368\t  - JUNO: \"Laser sight! Sniper on the lighthouse!\"\n1369\t  - THE GULL: \"Hold still, little agents.\"\n1370\t- **2-4**:\n1371\t  - CAPTOR: \"One more step and the old man swims!\"\n1372\t  - KAI: \"Easy… easy…\"\n1373\t  - DR. TEJADA: \"Mari! You came!\"\n1374\t  - MARI: \"Papa—get down!\"\n1375\t- **2-B**:\n1376\t  - HAMMERHEAD: \"LITTLE AGENTS. BIG MISTAKE.\"\n1377\t  - ROOK: \"Minigun! Get down!\"\n1378\t  - KAI: \"Cover's gone—moving!\"\n1379\t  - HAMMERHEAD: \"MY DOOR! YOU BROKE MY DOOR!\"\n1380\t  - HAMMERHEAD, on defeat: \"HAMMERHEAD… FALLS… DOWN…\"\n1381\t- **2-Z outro**:\n1382\t  - DR. TEJADA: \"The override is in the Tidewall control tower. At the peak, Krake opens every gate.\"\n1383\t  - JUNO: \"Forty minutes to dawn. The maintenance tram can get you there.\"\n1384\t  - KAI: \"Then let's catch a ride.\"\n1385\t- **Briefing 3**:\n1386\t  - HALE: \"This is it, agents. Jam the gates, reach the tower, stop Krake.\"\n1387\t  - JUNO: \"And maybe don't fall in. The water's rising.\"\n1388\t- **3-0 intro**:\n1389\t  - KRAKE (screens): \"Look at the sea, CREST. It rises for me.\"\n1390\t  - KRAKE: \"At dawn, Port Lumen returns to the deep!\"\n1391\t  - KAI: \"Not on our watch.\"\n1392\t  - ROOK: \"Did you rehearse that?\"\n1393\t  - KAI: \"…Maybe.\"\n1394\t- **3-1**:\n1395\t  - JUNO: \"Drones! Use the machine gun!\"\n1396\t  - JUNO: \"Rocket! Shoot it down!\"\n1397\t  - ROOK: \"Grenade launcher. My kind of party.\"\n1398\t- **3-2**:\n1399\t  - DR. TEJADA (radio): \"Jam the gate locks! Four of them—the glowing clamps!\"\n1400\t  - JUNO: \"Gunship inbound! It's the Seawolf!\"\n1401\t  - DR. TEJADA: \"Gate jammed! Hurry to the tower!\"\n1402\t- **3-3**:\n1403\t  - ROOK: \"Turbine hall. Mind the fans.\"\n1404\t  - JUNO: \"Coolant tanks—stay clear. Unless the bad guys are closer.\"\n1405\t- **3-4**:\n1406\t  - KAI: \"Going up.\"\n1407\t  - JUNO: \"Seawolf's back! Hit the weapon pods!\"\n1408\t  - ROOK: \"Scratch one gunship.\"\n1409\t- **3-B**:\n1410\t  - KRAKE: \"You climbed my tower. Admirable. Now meet my Scylla.\"\n1411\t  - JUNO: \"It's down! Hit the cockpit!\"\n1412\t  - KRAKE: \"You think a machine is my only weapon? I am the storm!\"\n1413\t  - DR. TEJADA: \"He's going for the master lever—stop him!\"\n1414\t  - HUD: \"FINAL SHOT!\"\n1415\t  - KRAKE: \"The sea… always… wins…\"\n1416\t  - KAI: \"Not today.\"\n1417\t- **Ending**:\n1418\t  - JUNO: \"All forty gates closing! You did it!\"\n1419\t  - MARI: \"Silas Krake, you're under arrest by the Lumen Coast Guard.\"\n1420\t  - KRAKE: \"The tide will turn again.\"\n1421\t  - ROOK: \"Twice a day. It's called science.\"\n1422\t  - HALE: \"Outstanding work, agents. Port Lumen owes you its dawn.\"\n1423\t  - KAI: \"Tell the festival to save us some lanterns.\"\n1424\t  - ROOK: \"Kid. No puns at the debriefing.\"\n1425\t  - KAI: \"No promises.\"\n1426\t  - THE END.\n1427\t- **Intel bottles** (6, shown in RECORDS → INTEL), for example:\n1428\t  - \"Note to self: never trust a fish that winks. —J.\"\n1429\t  - \"Krake's coffee order: black, like the Current. Two sugars.\"\n1430\t\n1431\t### 5.10 Art list\n1432\t- **New materials** (`E.MATERIALS` and `E.PATTERNS`):\n1433\t  - `corrugated` (container walls; vertical ridges), with four container colors;\n1434\t  - `concrete`, `asphalt`;\n1435\t  - `grate` (catwalks; `alphaTest`), `hazard` (diagonal stripes);\n1436\t  - `tarp`, `awning-stripe` (red and white, blue and white);\n1437\t  - `paper-lantern` (emissive with a warm ramp), `glass-lit` (emissive windows), `screen` (canvas texture);\n1438\t  - `wet` (an overlay that brightens lit bands);\n1439\t  - `sea-night`, `sea-storm`, `sea-dawn` (water);\n1440\t  - `rope`, `net` (`alphaTest`), `rubber`, `camo`;\n1441\t  - `signboard` (canvas text: \"PORT LUMEN FISH MARKET\", \"BERTH 9\", \"GULL'S REST\", \"TIDEWALL CONTROL\", \"DANGER — SLUICE\").\n1442\t  - From the engine library, reuse `planks`, `crate`, `brick`, `cobble`, `stone`, `slate`, `shingle`, `timber`,\n1443\t    `plaster`, `tiles`, `iron`, `steel`, `rusted`, `sand` and `rock`.\n1444\t- **Prefabs** (helpers on `G`, written as shape entries where they are still objects):\n1445\t  - Stage 1: `pier`, `quay`, `warehouse` (doors, windows, sign), `stall` (canopy, lanterns, goods), `lanternString`,\n1446\t    `fishingBoat`, `speedboat` (the player's carrier, with gunwale cover), `container`, `containerStack`,\n1447\t    `gantryCrane`, `forklift`, `marketHall` (with a gallery that can collapse), `canal` (walls, bridges, a low bridge),\n1448\t    `fireworksBarge`;\n1449\t  - Stage 2: `house` (timber or plaster, slate roof, breakable windows), `lane` (cobble, steps), `cart`, `well`,\n1450\t    `washingLine`, `netLoft` (stairs, roof hatch), `cliff` (rock meshes from `E.shapeMesh('rock', { params })`),\n1451\t    `funicular` (track and two cars), `lighthouse` (a tessellated tower, the gallery, the rotating lens, the beam),\n1452\t    `keeperHouse`;\n1453\t  - Stage 3: `seawall`, `gateHouse`, `sluiceGate` (with lock clamps), `catwalk` (rails), `turbine` (rotating),\n1454\t    `steamVent`, `controlTower`, `glassLift` (the carrier), `console` (emissive screens), `masterLever`, `helipad`;\n1455\t  - shared: `sandbags`, `barricade`, `lamppost` (static light), `bollard`, `explosiveBarrel` (red with a hazard label),\n1456\t    `ammoCrate` (orange), `lifeRing` (a red and white torus as a lathe), `intelBottle`, `sign`, `skyline` (low-poly far\n1457\t    buildings), `screen` (the giant broadcast screens).\n1458\t- **Vehicles and mechs** (mesh rigs posed by code): Stingray (hull, bridge, 2 turrets, a deck rail), jet ski, Bulldog\n1459\t  (with a turret), Seawolf (body, rotors, 2 pods), Scylla (body, 6 legs × 3 segments, 2 claws, 2 pods, cockpit),\n1460\t  drones (a box, 4 rotor discs, a red eye).\n1461\t- **Sprites** (`E.sprite` strings): weapon icons (4); bullet pips; life badges; the threat \"!\"; the reticles (3 styles);\n1462\t  the hit marker; an ammo crate icon; the life-ring icon; the bottle icon; debris chips; casings.\n1463\t- **Effects**:\n1464\t  - muzzle flashes (4 sizes; the player's at the bottom right);\n1465\t  - impact sparks, splinters, dust, glass shards, water splashes;\n1466\t  - tracers, laser beams, smoke trails;\n1467\t  - explosions: a fireball core, smoke columns, debris, a shock ring, a scorch decal;\n1468\t  - fire on barrels and lanterns; fireworks (peony, willow, ring); rain and splashes; steam; foam; sparks on drones;\n1469\t  - the lighthouse beam; dust under the Scylla's feet; the Seawolf's rotor wash on the water.\n1470\t\n1471\t### 5.11 Animation list (all on the engine's procedural rig, plus our post-process joint layers)\n1472\t- **Enemies**:\n1473\t  - pop up from a crouch (blending the `crouch` pose out while `point: true`);\n1474\t  - lean out (a joint layer); side step;\n1475\t  - roll (`flip`); vault (an arc with `air`); jump down (`air`, then `land`); rappel (`climb` on a rope line);\n1476\t  - run, and run-and-gun (`point` while running);\n1477\t  - kneel and fire (`kneel` with `point`);\n1478\t  - throw (the `throw` move); shoulder a launcher; reload (left hand to the magazine, a custom attack spec);\n1479\t  - shield walk (a stance with the shield forward); rusher slashes (`slash`, `overhead`, `backslash`, with long winds);\n1480\t  - surprise (`expr: 'shout'`).\n1481\t- **Reactions**: flinch (`hurt`); stagger (knockback and a lean); a headshot snap (a joint layer); the 5 death styles\n1482\t  of §4.6.\n1483\t- **Allies and NPCs**: run, point, cover crouch, `cheer` on stage clear, `hips` (Rook), `wave` (Mari to her father);\n1484\t  civilians panic (run with arms up as a joint layer, then crouch with hands over their heads).\n1485\t- **Bosses**:\n1486\t  - Barracuda: aims the harpoon gun; ducks behind the bridge; swings on a rope (a pendulum path with `air`); cutlass\n1487\t    combo (`slash`, `backslash`, `thrust`); falls backwards into the sea;\n1488\t  - Hammerhead: shield bash; minigun spin-up and sweep (the torso twists); grenade toss; a charge (`sprint` lean); a\n1489\t    kneeling stagger; a fall through the railing;\n1490\t  - Krake: twin flare pistols; a dodge roll; a cutlass lunge; a dramatic point (`expr: 'angry'`); the lever lunge; a\n1491\t    defeat stagger to the window.\n1492\t- **Machines**: the Scylla's IK gait (tripod, alternating), claw aim, topple and get-up; turret spin-up and tracking;\n1493\t  Seawolf bank and strafe; jet-ski bounce; boat bobbing; turbines turning; sluice gates moving; the lens turning.\n1494\t- **Camera**: cover duck and pop; recoil; hit jolt; arrival whip-pans; travel bob; carrier sway; cutscene moves;\n1495\t  slow-motion final shot; boss reveal.\n1496\t\n1497\t### 5.12 Music and SFX (written as code)\n1498\t| Song | Use | Feel |\n1499\t|---|---|---|\n1500\t| `theme` | title, attract | 140 bpm in D minor: a rising \"wave\" arpeggio motif, a brassy pulse lead, saw octave bass, rock drums |\n1501\t| `briefing` | briefings, the hub card | 90 bpm, a tense pad (triangle and pulse12), a ticking hi-hat |\n1502\t| `harbor` | Stage 1 | 150 bpm, festival latin-rock: tresillo bass, square lead, clave-like drums; layers `drums` and `lead` |\n1503\t| `storm` | Stage 2 | 160 bpm, driving minor, galloping bass, noise \"thunder\" hits |\n1504\t| `tidewall` | Stage 3 | 155 bpm, heroic, modulating up a step at 3-3 |\n1505\t| `boss` | 1-B, 2-B, mini-bosses | 170 bpm, aggressive |\n1506\t| `kingtide` | the final boss | 165 bpm, epic; tempo up for the FINAL SHOT |\n1507\t| `range` | Training | light funk |\n1508\t| `results` / `clear` (sting) / `continue` / `gameover` / `ending` (a slow ballad version of `theme`) | | |\n1509\t\n1510\t**SFX**:\n1511\t- the 4 weapons; empty click; reload; switching;\n1512\t- cover in and out (a cloth whoosh, a thud);\n1513\t- whizz; ricochet; impacts on metal, wood, concrete, water and glass; enemy hit, headshot \"ding\" and death barks;\n1514\t- the threat tick and chirp; the TIME tick, TIME EXTEND, TIDE'S IN;\n1515\t- ammo pickup, 1UP, NEW WEAPON;\n1516\t- explosions (small and big), barrel and tank fire;\n1517\t- grenade bounce; rocket whoosh; harpoon twang; torpedo hiss; missile; flare pop;\n1518\t- turret spin-up; the minigun; the Scylla's stomp and servo; rotor; jet ski; boat engine;\n1519\t- glass break, lantern burn, wood break;\n1520\t- UI: move, confirm, back, a rank stamp, count-up ticks.\n1521\t\n1522\t---\n1523\t\n1524\t## 6. Build order and milestones\n1525\tEvery milestone ends with: its tests green in `node tests/run.mjs`, the bundle building, and `tools/check.mjs` free of\n1526\terrors.\n1527\t\n1528\t| # | Milestone | Done when (acceptance) |\n1529\t|---|---|---|\n1530\t| **M0** | **Setup.** The dev folder, the engine copy, the tools, `hub/` files, `package.json`, `build.mjs`, `run.mjs`, a title text in the bundle | The bundle opens from `file://` with no errors; the build test passes (meta order, session client byte-identical, hub tags, no external URLs); the runner prints its count line |\n1531\t| **M1** | **Renderer spike** (the biggest risk; do it first). math3d, the texture bank, a textured and lit box room with a floor, water and sky, an `E.shapeMesh` crate, **a Humanoid billboard half-hidden behind the crate**, a corridor that tests near clipping, a muzzle-flash light | Unit tests for projection round trips, near clipping (no NaN, 0–2 triangles), the z-test, and billboard compositing on synthetic pixels; 3 screenshots (actor at 6, 12 and 24 m) look right |\n1532\t| **M2** | **The core loop** in a grey-box version of 1-1. Sim and commands, RailCam slots and cover, aim (mouse, pad, keys), the handgun and reload, `deckhand` with peeks, the ThreatDirector and the crisis flash, lives, TIME, clear → WAIT → travel → the next scene, the HUD basics, basic SFX | Tests: the cover timings and `exposed`; no firing in cover; fire in cover switches weapons; reload; rays hit the head and torso and are blocked by cover; threats hit exposed players and are blocked in cover; pop-out protection; TIME counts only in ACTION; time-up; the scene flow |\n1533\t| **M3** | **Combat roster.** All 4 weapons, every archetype with its entries, reactions and deaths, projectiles, breakables, barrels, pickups, civilians, allies; **engine patch 1** (the long guns) | One scripted test per archetype and per object; filmstrips of the pop-up, the deaths and the rusher's slash |\n1534\t| **M3.5** | **Net spike.** Host and replica with a FakeHub in Node on the grey-box scene; a minimal session build | The net suite passes at 2 and 4 players with latency, jitter and loss; the harness passes `players=2` and `scenario=server` |\n1535\t| **M4** | **Stage 1 complete**: the geometry and look, scenes 1-1…1-4, Bulldog, the Stingray/Barracuda boss, cutscenes and briefings, **the voice synth**, music and SFX, results, continue, game over and initials | The content validators pass; the `fair` bot clears Stage 1 on Normal; cutscenes run headless to the end, and skipping works; screenshots of every scene |\n1536\t| **M5** | **Stage 2 complete**: rain and lightning, the funicular, The Gull, shields, rushers, the hostage, Hammerhead with degrading cover | As M4, for Stage 2 |\n1537\t| **M6** | **Stage 3 complete**: drones, rockets, the GL, the sluice locks, Seawolf, the turbines, the lift, Scylla, Krake, the FINAL SHOT, the ending and the credits | As M4; the `--playthrough` cheat run reaches the ending and writes records |\n1538\t| **M7** | **Front end and attract**: the title flyover, menus, difficulty, select, briefing, Training, records, about, how-to, settings items, device-aware prompts, glyph patch 2, wheel patch 3, the touch-only notice, the attract cycle | UI flow tests; attract tests (10 s idle → demo, input → title, the playlist cycles, the watchdog); prompt tests per device and glyph family |\n1539\t| **M8** | **Dev mode**: the panel, every slider, toggle and action, the overlays, the free camera, reset | Each slider changes `tune`; reset restores `TUNE` exactly; each action works (tested) |\n1540\t| **M9** | **Local co-op**: join, split screen, per-player HUD, continues | Co-op tests: two cameras, independent cover and hits, pickups to the killer, continues per player |\n1541\t| **M10** | **Full AI Hub integration**: our own card, stats and awards, every scenario | All 4 harness scenarios pass (`__hubCheck.pass`); the game still runs outside a session |\n1542\t| **M11** | **Polish and balance**: juice, the audio mix, the `fair` bot's balance (`tests/balance.json`), screenshot reviews at 16:9, 4:3 and 21:9, `About` data, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | The §9 checklist is all ticked; `--all` is green |\n1543\t\n1544\t**Cut order, if time runs short.** Cut whole scenes, never mechanics. The validators must pass after each cut.\n1545\t1. 3-4 Tower Lift: the Seawolf's finale moves into the end of 3-2.\n1546\t2. 2-2 Net Lofts: the shield and the rappellers move into 2-1 and 2-4.\n1547\t3. 1-3 Container Yard: the Bulldog moves into 1-2's street exit.\n1548\t4. The intel bottles.\n1549\t5. The allies' appearances in single player.\n1550\t\n1551\t---\n1552\t\n1553\t## 7. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1554\t| Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |\n1555\t|---|---|---|\n1556\t| **The software renderer** (correctness, look, speed) | It is the largest piece of new code, and everything depends on it | M1 comes first, with unit tests for projection, clipping, depth and compositing, and screenshots. Use typed arrays and no allocations in inner loops; cull by chunk and per object; tessellate big faces; give the dev perf overlay ms per pass. Fallbacks: affine spans of 16 px; a lower internal resolution for the 3D pass only |\n1557\t| **Rig billboards in perspective** (scale, angle, ground contact, night light) | The engine draws rigs orthographically, from views that can't look up | Bearing-based yaw per actor; pitch clamped to 3° or more; a chest-depth bias; blob shadows; light per actor with a floor of 0.45. Filmstrips at 3 distances and bearings in M1 and M3 |\n1558\t| **Hit fidelity** (what you see vs what you hit) | Players feel every miss | Hit volumes from the rig's joints every step; the dev \"show hit volumes\" overlay; tests that aim at `rig.J.head` and expect HEADSHOT |\n1559\t| **Pad aiming feel** | A light gun on a stick feels slow | The response curve, acceleration and aim assist (friction and magnetism), all as sliders; the `fair` bot's time-to-target as a metric; early hands-on tests in M2 |\n1560\t| **Threat fairness** | Unreadable damage kills the genre | Telegraphs read by shape, sound and arrow; `maxThreats`, `minGap`, pop-out protection; tests that inject overlapping threats |\n1561\t| **Content volume** (3 stages) | Big, and easy to leave half-done | Prefabs, data scenes, validators, the free camera with Copy pose; finish Stage 1 completely before starting Stage 2; the cut order in §6 |\n1562\t| **Netcode and hub compliance** | Latency and loss, the server and host-leave scenarios | The M3.5 spike; FakeHub tests in Node (rates, sizes, standings, leave, time-up); the real harness in Chromium; the host authoritative and the replica cosmetic |\n1563\t| **Engine patches regressing the engine** | Shared code | Small, documented patches (`PATCHES.md`), each with a test; `node kits/test.mjs brawler` and `shooter` from the handoff copy still pass |\n1564\t| **The single-file bundle** | Script order, the session client first, size | The build test parses the output; `check.mjs` opens it from `file://` |\n1565\t| **The attract bot getting stuck** | An endless loop on a kiosk | Cheats on, the watchdog, a highlight timeout, tests over the whole playlist |\n1566\t| **Voice synth timing and CPU** | Many nodes | Schedule ahead in the audio clock; at most 2 dialog voices and 4 barks; a headless no-op path; the dev Voice test |\n1567\t| **Determinism drift** | Breaks the tests, the replays and the net rewind | Seeded streams per system; a test greps the sim files for `Math.random`; a test that the same seed and commands give the same `sim.hash()` |\n1568\t| **`/tmp` full** | Browsers fail with misleading errors | `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for every browser tool (§0.3) |\n1569\t\n1570\t---\n1571\t\n1572\t## 8. Testing\n1573\t\n1574\t### 8.1 The one command\n1575\t`node tests/run.mjs [suite …] [--playthrough] [--browser] [--hub] [--all]`\n1576\t- It loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `build/game.js` into a fresh `vm` context for each suite (the pattern of the\n1577\t  handoff's `game/test.mjs`), headless, where `draw` is skipped. It rebuilds `build/game.js` first if any `src/` file\n1578\t  is newer.\n1579\t- Each suite is `export default async t => { … }`, using:\n1580\t  - `t.check(name, ok, detail)`;\n1581\t  - `t.load({ seed, mode })` → `{ E, game, debug }`;\n1582\t  - `t.step(seconds)`, which wraps `game.advance`;\n1583\t  - helpers `aimAt(world point, player)`, `fire`, `cover`.\n1584\t- **The output is only `FAIL suite › check: detail` lines, then one line, `N passed, M failed (T s)`.** The exit code\n1585\t  is 1 on any failure.\n1586\t- `game.debug`:\n1587\t  - `snapshot()`: scene, phase, stage, scene id, timer, players, enemies, threats, boss, errors;\n1588\t  - `jump`, `cheat`, `bot(on, style)`, `aimAt`, `fire`, `cover`;\n1589\t  - `sim` and `tune`.\n1590\t- Every suite ends by checking that `game.errors` is empty.\n1591\t\n1592\t### 8.2 Suites (what each part is tested by)\n1593\t| Suite | Checks |\n1594\t|---|---|\n1595\t| `build` | `<meta charset>` comes first, then the session client (sha256 equal to `hub/session.js`), then the hub tags (goal ≤ 60 characters, howto ≤ 80); the engine before the game; no `http(s)://` fetches; `exit-interview.json` parses and has every key |\n1596\t| `math3d` | project and unproject round trips; aim → ray → aim; ray vs box, sphere and capsule; the yaw and pitch conventions (yaw 0 looks east, right is +y) |\n1597\t| `raster` | near-plane clipping cases; the depth test (a near quad hides a far one in a 16×16 buffer); band dithering stays in range; billboard compositing with depth; fog quantization |\n1598\t| `materials` | every material builds 5 distinct bands; the lid variants; the canvas textures headless-safe |\n1599\t| `geometry` | `E.shapeMesh` import; prefabs give colliders; `TC.H.rig` is 24–30 u |\n1600\t| `content` | every validator in §4.10, over every stage |\n1601\t| `input` | `label()` per device and glyph family (PlayStation by default, Xbox via the setting); wheel codes; pointer → aim exact; pad curve, acceleration and assist (friction near a target, none on civilians) |\n1602\t| `cover` | blend timings; `exposed`; hold vs toggle; reload in cover; fire in cover switches weapons |\n1603\t| `weapons` | fire rates; magazine and pools; pellets; GL splash and falloff; the bloom; switch times; ammo carried over; auto-switch when empty |\n1604\t| `player` | lives; i-frames; continue (score reset, the mark); extra lives at the thresholds; the life ring |\n1605\t| `timer` | counts only in ACTION and boss; TIME EXTEND; TIDE'S IN; the refill; the clear bonus |\n1606\t| `scoring` | points by event; the chain growing, capping and resetting; the ranks |\n1607\t| `enemies` | one scripted scenario per archetype: its entry, peek and fire plan, death by every style, the quartermaster's drop and flight, shield immunity and knock-aside, the rusher's slash vs cover, the sniper's laser, drones, jet skis, the captor and hostage |\n1608\t| `threats` | `maxThreats`, `minGap`, pop-out protection, always-threat kinds, the ring timing, misses never damaging |\n1609\t| `projectiles` | each kind shootable; grenade, rocket and missile blocked by cover; the torpedo not blocked; explosions damaging enemies only |\n1610\t| `objects` | barrel chains; breakables removing colliders; the civilian penalty; allies passing shots through; bottles going to INTEL |\n1611\t| `bosses` | each boss: phases advance on scripted damage (`debug.fire` at its parts), cover degradation and the swap, the topple and cockpit, the FINAL SHOT hit and miss paths, defeat → outro |\n1612\t| `story` | every cutscene runs headless to its end; skipping lands on the same end state; every speaker and voice exists; voice durations are positive |\n1613\t| `audio` | every song parses (each track has a whole number of steps); every SFX name exists; layers by phase |\n1614\t| `ui` | title → menu → ARCADE → difficulty → briefing → play → pause → Dev mode → reset → quit to title; results → initials → records; About pages are complete with no empty fields; the touch-only notice (stubbed `matchMedia`) |\n1615\t| `dev` | each slider changes its `tune` path; reset restores `TUNE` deep-equal; each action works |\n1616\t| `attract` | 10 s idle → demo; any input → title (consumed); the playlist cycles; the watchdog advances |\n1617\t| `coop` | P2 joins; 2 viewports; independent cameras and cover; separate hits and continues; pickups to the killer |\n1618\t| `net` | FakeHub (injectable `hub` object): 1, 2 and 4 players; latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5%; server mode; host leave; time-up → `finish` with valid standings and scores; ≤ 20 messages a second per copy; every `s` ≤ 1,200 bytes; kills credited to the right player; replicas converge |\n1619\t| `determinism` | the same seed and commands give the same `sim.hash()` after 60 s; no `Math.random` in sim files; no hardcoded key names in prompts |\n1620\t| `--playthrough` | the `fair` bot clears Stages 1, 2 and 3 on Normal without a continue (and records the time per scene to `tests/balance.json`, which the content suite reads); the `showoff` cheat bot plays the whole ARCADE to the credits and the initials; the Training range completes |\n1621\t| `--browser` | `tools/check.mjs` on the bundle at 1920×1080, 1280×720, 2560×1080 and 1024×768: no errors, the canvas filled, screenshots of the title, 1-1, a boss and split screen |\n1622\t| `--hub` | `tools/hubcheck.mjs` copies the bundle and the harness files into `hubtest/`, serves it on `127.0.0.1:0`, confirms the page is ours, then runs `harness.html?game=…&players=2&auto=1`, `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, and `…&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. It waits for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, reads `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and prints only the failed checks. It kills its server by PID |\n1623\t\n1624\t### 8.3 What only eyes can check (screenshots and filmstrips)\n1625\t- The M1 renderer spike.\n1626\t- One screenshot per scene; every boss in each phase.\n1627\t- The HUD at 16:9, 4:3 and 21:9; split screen; the title and menus; the attract overlay; the touch-only notice.\n1628\t- Filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`): the cover duck, an enemy pop-up, each death style, the rusher's slash,\n1629\t  Hammerhead's sweep, the Scylla's gait and topple, every engine weapon pose.\n1630\t\n1631\tRerun only after changing what they show.\n1632\t\n1633\t---\n1634\t\n1635\t## 9. Done checklist (TASK.md → where it's covered)\n1636\t- [ ] **Title** picked by RNG from 50 riffs: Tide Crisis 3 (the top of this plan).\n1637\t- [ ] **Genre and perspective** chosen: an on-rails light-gun shooter with cover, in first person (§1).\n1638\t- [ ] **The single HTML** and the dev folder with the exact names; plays from `file://` (§0.1, §3.2).\n1639\t- [ ] **Built on the handoff engine**; the changes logged in `engine/PATCHES.md` (§3.6).\n1640\t- [ ] **Art** in the engine's native style with new assets (§4.1, §5.10); **animation** on the engine's rigs with new\n1641\t      moves (§5.11).\n1642\t- [ ] **Audio** all in code: music, SFX and gibberish voices (§4.12, §5.12).\n1643\t- [ ] **Online**: AI Hub shared-world co-op, all 4 harness scenarios pass (§4.19); **multiplayer on its own**: local\n1644\t      split-screen co-op (§4.18).\n1645\t- [ ] **Every mechanic** shown in the demo:\n1646\t  - cover and reload; 4 weapons and switching; quartermaster ammo; the crisis flash;\n1647\t  - Red Tide; grenades, rockets, torpedoes, missiles and flares shot down;\n1648\t  - shields, rushers, snipers, drones, jet skis, vehicles, hostages, civilians;\n1649\t  - breakables and barrels; life rings and intel; TIME, TIME EXTEND and TIDE'S IN;\n1650\t  - chain, ranks, continues, initials;\n1651\t  - moving scenes; 3 bosses, 3 mini-bosses and the FINAL SHOT;\n1652\t  - Training (§5).\n1653\t- [ ] **Dev mode** from the pause menu: live sliders, toggles, actions, reset to defaults (§4.16).\n1654\t- [ ] **Attract mode** after 10 s idle on the title or menu, a looping AI demo, any input exits (§4.17).\n1655\t- [ ] **10-foot, controller-first UI**:\n1656\t  - DualSense mapping; native keyboard and mouse (the mouse aims and its hover moves the focus);\n1657\t  - prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option;\n1658\t  - no dense screens (§4.3, §4.13–4.15).\n1659\t- [ ] **Touch-only**: \"Controller or keyboard required\" with the settings button, and the attract mode runs (§4.14).\n1660\t- [ ] **Narrative tone** in the source's B-movie style, with every beat scripted (§5.2, §5.9).\n1661\t- [ ] **Tests**: one command printing only failures and a count; a scripted playthrough of the whole game; headless\n1662\t      `game.advance`/`game.debug` (§8).\n1663\t- [ ] **No TODOs, placeholders or stubs.** A last check:\n1664\t      `grep -rniE \"todo|fixme|placeholder|lorem|stub\" src/` returns nothing.\n1665\t- [ ] **About/Credits screen** with Source Information, Testing Feedback (4), Engine Feedback (6) and Prompt Feedback\n1666\t      (4) (§4.14).\n1667\t- [ ] **`exit-interview.json`** in the exact shape, every value filled (\"unknown\" where unconfirmed), parsed by a test.\n1668\t      Suggested `aiHub` block:\n1669\t      `{ \"name\": \"Tide Crisis 3\", \"tagline\": \"Duck. Pop. Shoot. Beat the tide.\", \"description\": \"An original arcade light-gun rail shooter in PS1-style pixel 3D: duck behind cover, switch between four weapons and race each area's clock to retake an island's tidal barrier before the dawn king tide. Play solo, couch co-op or AI Hub co-op for up to four.\", \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Shooter\", \"source\": \"Time Crisis 3\", \"series\": \"Time Crisis\", \"players\": \"1–4\", \"controls\": \"Mouse or stick aims · left click/R2 fires · hold right click/L2 for cover and reload · wheel/R1 switches weapons\", \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"arcade\", \"co-op\", \"boss fights\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\"] }`\n1670\t- [ ] **The final chat reply** repeats Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n1671\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14efaf47-c831-41be-b2ba-0398106a097f","uuid":"ada02f9b-76cd-4708-a428-251c2b7802f9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:33.535Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183213__xf5fb84/work/PLAN.md","content":"  itself, limping. A second topple, from the remaining knees, breaks the cockpit open and Krake ejects.\n\n**ADMIRAL KRAKE** (3-B, phase 2, 90 s; 40 HP):\n- He rolls and dashes between the control-room consoles.\n- He fires **flares** with both pistols: slow, glowing, shootable, bursting into firework sparks.\n- He throws smoke, which cuts visibility to 40% for 3 s.\n- He summons 2 Red Tide at a time.\n- **FINAL SHOT.** At 15% HP he lunges for the master sluice lever. Slow motion (presentation timeScale 0.3) and a\n  3-second ring show over the lever arm; hitting the arm or the lever wins. A miss means he pulls it partway: the water\n  surges, \"TIDE RISING!\", and the fight resumes; repeat until it lands.\n- **Defeat**: \"The sea… always… wins…\" Kai: \"Not today.\" Then the ending.\n\n**Mini-bosses**: **BULLDOG** (1-3), **THE GULL** (2-3) and **SEAWOLF** (3-2 and 3-4) are registered as bosses with an\nHP bar but no intro card.\n\n### 5.8 Training: the CREST RANGE (Juno instructs)\nAn indoor range of concrete lanes with dividers, plywood cut-outs of Black Current goons on rails, and score lamps.\n1. **AIM & FIRE**: 6 pop-up cut-outs at 8–15 m. \"AIM [stick/mouse] · FIRE [R2/Left click]\".\n2. **COVER & RELOAD**: a turret robot (a box with a red lamp) telegraphs 3 shots; hide for each. Then empty the\n   magazine and reload in cover. \"HOLD [L2] TO TAKE COVER — YOU RELOAD IN COVER\".\n3. **WEAPONS**: shoot an orange-vest cut-out for MG ammo, switch with [R1], shred 3 drone targets; a shotgun on a\n   shield cut-out; the GL on a crate stack. \"[R1]/[L1] — OR FIRE WHILE IN COVER — TO SWITCH\".\n4. **READ THE CRISIS**: a Red Tide cut-out (a fast telegraph), a grenade lob (shoot it), a civilian cut-out (\"DON'T\n   SHOOT\"), then a timed drill: 8 targets in 20 s, with the TIME HUD.\n\n\"TRAINING COMPLETE\" records the best time. The first ARCADE start offers Training once (and `seenTraining` remembers).\n\n### 5.9 Script (every story beat; the lines are original)\n- **Briefing 1** (HQ):\n  - HALE: \"Agents. Two hours ago the Black Current seized Port Lumen's harbor and the Tidewall.\"\n  - HALE: \"Their leader is Silas Krake. A disgraced admiral with a grudge the size of an ocean.\"\n  - JUNO: \"He'll open the floodgates at dawn. King tide. The whole city goes under.\"\n  - HALE: \"You have until 06:00. Land at Lantern Pier. Find his signal. End this.\"\n  - KAI: \"Understood. CREST is on it.\"\n- **1-0 intro**:\n  - MARI: \"Hang on! Lumen Coast Guard express—next stop, trouble!\"\n  - KRAKE (screens): \"Citizens of Port Lumen! Enjoy your lanterns. They are the last lights you will see.\"\n  - KRAKE: \"At dawn the king tide comes, and I open every gate. The sea takes back what you stole!\"\n  - ROOK: \"Charming guy.\"\n  - KAI: \"Let's make some waves.\"\n  - ROOK: \"Kid, you say that every mission.\"\n- **1-1**:\n  - JUNO: \"Hostiles on the pier! Watch the festival crowd!\"\n  - JUNO, at the quartermaster: \"Orange vest! He's hauling ammo—drop him!\"\n  - KAI, on the clear: \"Pier's clear. Moving!\"\n- **1-2**:\n  - ROOK: \"Market hall. Stay sharp.\"\n  - JUNO: \"Red uniform! That's Red Tide—they don't miss. Hit him first!\"\n  - JUNO: \"Grenade! Shoot it out of the air!\"\n  - ROOK, when the gallery falls: \"Now that's what I call fresh fish.\"\n- **1-3**:\n  - JUNO: \"Something big is coming through the containers!\"\n  - KAI: \"Armored truck! Take out the gunner!\"\n  - ROOK: \"Fuel tank—light it up!\"\n  - WORKER: \"Don't shoot! I just work here!\"\n- **1-4**:\n  - MARI: \"Grab something! We're taking the canals!\"\n  - JUNO: \"Jet skis, three o'clock!\"\n  - MARI: \"Low bridge! Heads down!\"\n  - ROOK: \"Fireworks barge. Happy festival.\"\n- **1-B**:\n  - BARRACUDA: \"CREST! The Admiral said you'd come. He didn't say you'd be this slow!\"\n  - BARRACUDA: \"Say hello to the Stingray!\"\n  - BARRACUDA, phase 3: \"Enough! I'll do this myself!\"\n  - MARI: \"Torpedo in the water! Shoot it!\"\n  - BARRACUDA, on defeat: \"This isn't over, CREST!\"\n- **1-Z outro**:\n  - JUNO: \"Krake's signal is coming from Lighthouse Point.\"\n  - MARI: \"Gull's Rest. They've held my father there since yesterday.\"\n  - KAI: \"Then that's where we're going.\"\n  - ROOK: \"Into a storm. Naturally.\"\n- **Briefing 2**:\n  - HALE: \"The lighthouse relays Krake's commands to the whole fleet.\"\n  - JUNO: \"Take it out and his ships go deaf. Also, it's raining. A lot.\"\n- **2-0 intro**:\n  - KRAKE (intercept): \"Hammerhead. No one reaches the lamp.\"\n  - HAMMERHEAD: \"NOBODY. PASSES. HAMMERHEAD.\"\n  - ROOK: \"He talks in capital letters.\"\n- **2-1**:\n  - JUNO: \"Blades! Don't let them get close!\"\n  - KAI: \"Shotgun. Now we're talking.\"\n  - FISHERMAN: \"Not me! Not me!\"\n- **2-2**:\n  - JUNO: \"Shield! Knock it aside with the shotgun!\"\n  - ROOK: \"Ropes! They're coming through the roof!\"\n- **2-3**:\n  - MARI: \"The funicular's the only way up the cliff.\"\n  - JUNO: \"Car coming down—it's full of them!\"\n  - JUNO: \"Laser sight! Sniper on the lighthouse!\"\n  - THE GULL: \"Hold still, little agents.\"\n- **2-4**:\n  - CAPTOR: \"One more step and the old man swims!\"\n  - KAI: \"Easy… easy…\"\n  - DR. TEJADA: \"Mari! You came!\"\n  - MARI: \"Papa—get down!\"\n- **2-B**:\n  - HAMMERHEAD: \"LITTLE AGENTS. BIG MISTAKE.\"\n  - ROOK: \"Minigun! Get down!\"\n  - KAI: \"Cover's gone—moving!\"\n  - HAMMERHEAD: \"MY DOOR! YOU BROKE MY DOOR!\"\n  - HAMMERHEAD, on defeat: \"HAMMERHEAD… FALLS… DOWN…\"\n- **2-Z outro**:\n  - DR. TEJADA: \"The override is in the Tidewall control tower. At the peak, Krake opens every gate.\"\n  - JUNO: \"Forty minutes to dawn. The maintenance tram can get you there.\"\n  - KAI: \"Then let's catch a ride.\"\n- **Briefing 3**:\n  - HALE: \"This is it, agents. Jam the gates, reach the tower, stop Krake.\"\n  - JUNO: \"And maybe don't fall in. The water's rising.\"\n- **3-0 intro**:\n  - KRAKE (screens): \"Look at the sea, CREST. It rises for me.\"\n  - KRAKE: \"At dawn, Port Lumen returns to the deep!\"\n  - KAI: \"Not on our watch.\"\n  - ROOK: \"Did you rehearse that?\"\n  - KAI: \"…Maybe.\"\n- **3-1**:\n  - JUNO: \"Drones! Use the machine gun!\"\n  - JUNO: \"Rocket! Shoot it down!\"\n  - ROOK: \"Grenade launcher. My kind of party.\"\n- **3-2**:\n  - DR. TEJADA (radio): \"Jam the gate locks! Four of them—the glowing clamps!\"\n  - JUNO: \"Gunship inbound! It's the Seawolf!\"\n  - DR. TEJADA: \"Gate jammed! Hurry to the tower!\"\n- **3-3**:\n  - ROOK: \"Turbine hall. Mind the fans.\"\n  - JUNO: \"Coolant tanks—stay clear. Unless the bad guys are closer.\"\n- **3-4**:\n  - KAI: \"Going up.\"\n  - JUNO: \"Seawolf's back! Hit the weapon pods!\"\n  - ROOK: \"Scratch one gunship.\"\n- **3-B**:\n  - KRAKE: \"You climbed my tower. Admirable. Now meet my Scylla.\"\n  - JUNO: \"It's down! Hit the cockpit!\"\n  - KRAKE: \"You think a machine is my only weapon? I am the storm!\"\n  - DR. TEJADA: \"He's going for the master lever—stop him!\"\n  - HUD: \"FINAL SHOT!\"\n  - KRAKE: \"The sea… always… wins…\"\n  - KAI: \"Not today.\"\n- **Ending**:\n  - JUNO: \"All forty gates closing! You did it!\"\n  - MARI: \"Silas Krake, you're under arrest by the Lumen Coast Guard.\"\n  - KRAKE: \"The tide will turn again.\"\n  - ROOK: \"Twice a day. It's called science.\"\n  - HALE: \"Outstanding work, agents. Port Lumen owes you its dawn.\"\n  - KAI: \"Tell the festival to save us some lanterns.\"\n  - ROOK: \"Kid. No puns at the debriefing.\"\n  - KAI: \"No promises.\"\n  - THE END.\n- **Intel bottles** (6, shown in RECORDS → INTEL), for example:\n  - \"Note to self: never trust a fish that winks. —J.\"\n  - \"Krake's coffee order: black, like the Current. Two sugars.\"\n\n### 5.10 Art list\n- **New materials** (`E.MATERIALS` and `E.PATTERNS`):\n  - `corrugated` (container walls; vertical ridges), with four container colors;\n  - `concrete`, `asphalt`;\n  - `grate` (catwalks; `alphaTest`), `hazard` (diagonal stripes);\n  - `tarp`, `awning-stripe` (red and white, blue and white);\n  - `paper-lantern` (emissive with a warm ramp), `glass-lit` (emissive windows), `screen` (canvas texture);\n  - `wet` (an overlay that brightens lit bands);\n  - `sea-night`, `sea-storm`, `sea-dawn` (water);\n  - `rope`, `net` (`alphaTest`), `rubber`, `camo`;\n  - `signboard` (canvas text: \"PORT LUMEN FISH MARKET\", \"BERTH 9\", \"GULL'S REST\", \"TIDEWALL CONTROL\", \"DANGER — SLUICE\").\n  - From the engine library, reuse `planks`, `crate`, `brick`, `cobble`, `stone`, `slate`, `shingle`, `timber`,\n    `plaster`, `tiles`, `iron`, `steel`, `rusted`, `sand` and `rock`.\n- **Prefabs** (helpers on `G`, written as shape entries where they are still objects):\n  - Stage 1: `pier`, `quay`, `warehouse` (doors, windows, sign), `stall` (canopy, lanterns, goods), `lanternString`,\n    `fishingBoat`, `speedboat` (the player's carrier, with gunwale cover), `container`, `containerStack`,\n    `gantryCrane`, `forklift`, `marketHall` (with a gallery that can collapse), `canal` (walls, bridges, a low bridge),\n    `fireworksBarge`;\n  - Stage 2: `house` (timber or plaster, slate roof, breakable windows), `lane` (cobble, steps), `cart`, `well`,\n    `washingLine`, `netLoft` (stairs, roof hatch), `cliff` (rock meshes from `E.shapeMesh('rock', { params })`),\n    `funicular` (track and two cars), `lighthouse` (a tessellated tower, the gallery, the rotating lens, the beam),\n    `keeperHouse`;\n  - Stage 3: `seawall`, `gateHouse`, `sluiceGate` (with lock clamps), `catwalk` (rails), `turbine` (rotating),\n    `steamVent`, `controlTower`, `glassLift` (the carrier), `console` (emissive screens), `masterLever`, `helipad`;\n  - shared: `sandbags`, `barricade`, `lamppost` (static light), `bollard`, `explosiveBarrel` (red with a hazard label),\n    `ammoCrate` (orange), `lifeRing` (a red and white torus as a lathe), `intelBottle`, `sign`, `skyline` (low-poly far\n    buildings), `screen` (the giant broadcast screens).\n- **Vehicles and mechs** (mesh rigs posed by code): Stingray (hull, bridge, 2 turrets, a deck rail), jet ski, Bulldog\n  (with a turret), Seawolf (body, rotors, 2 pods), Scylla (body, 6 legs × 3 segments, 2 claws, 2 pods, cockpit),\n  drones (a box, 4 rotor discs, a red eye).\n- **Sprites** (`E.sprite` strings): weapon icons (4); bullet pips; life badges; the threat \"!\"; the reticles (3 styles);\n  the hit marker; an ammo crate icon; the life-ring icon; the bottle icon; debris chips; casings.\n- **Effects**:\n  - muzzle flashes (4 sizes; the player's at the bottom right);\n  - impact sparks, splinters, dust, glass shards, water splashes;\n  - tracers, laser beams, smoke trails;\n  - explosions: a fireball core, smoke columns, debris, a shock ring, a scorch decal;\n  - fire on barrels and lanterns; fireworks (peony, willow, ring); rain and splashes; steam; foam; sparks on drones;\n  - the lighthouse beam; dust under the Scylla's feet; the Seawolf's rotor wash on the water.\n\n### 5.11 Animation list (all on the engine's procedural rig, plus our post-process joint layers)\n- **Enemies**:\n  - pop up from a crouch (blending the `crouch` pose out while `point: true`);\n  - lean out (a joint layer); side step;\n  - roll (`flip`); vault (an arc with `air`); jump down (`air`, then `land`); rappel (`climb` on a rope line);\n  - run, and run-and-gun (`point` while running);\n  - kneel and fire (`kneel` with `point`);\n  - throw (the `throw` move); shoulder a launcher; reload (left hand to the magazine, a custom attack spec);\n  - shield walk (a stance with the shield forward); rusher slashes (`slash`, `overhead`, `backslash`, with long winds);\n  - surprise (`expr: 'shout'`).\n- **Reactions**: flinch (`hurt`); stagger (knockback and a lean); a headshot snap (a joint layer); the 5 death styles\n  of §4.6.\n- **Allies and NPCs**: run, point, cover crouch, `cheer` on stage clear, `hips` (Rook), `wave` (Mari to her father);\n  civilians panic (run with arms up as a joint layer, then crouch with hands over their heads).\n- **Bosses**:\n  - Barracuda: aims the harpoon gun; ducks behind the bridge; swings on a rope (a pendulum path with `air`); cutlass\n    combo (`slash`, `backslash`, `thrust`); falls backwards into the sea;\n  - Hammerhead: shield bash; minigun spin-up and sweep (the torso twists); grenade toss; a charge (`sprint` lean); a\n    kneeling stagger; a fall through the railing;\n  - Krake: twin flare pistols; a dodge roll; a cutlass lunge; a dramatic point (`expr: 'angry'`); the lever lunge; a\n    defeat stagger to the window.\n- **Machines**: the Scylla's IK gait (tripod, alternating), claw aim, topple and get-up; turret spin-up and tracking;\n  Seawolf bank and strafe; jet-ski bounce; boat bobbing; turbines turning; sluice gates moving; the lens turning.\n- **Camera**: cover duck and pop; recoil; hit jolt; arrival whip-pans; travel bob; carrier sway; cutscene moves;\n  slow-motion final shot; boss reveal.\n\n### 5.12 Music and SFX (written as code)\n| Song | Use | Feel |\n|---|---|---|\n| `theme` | title, attract | 140 bpm in D minor: a rising \"wave\" arpeggio motif, a brassy pulse lead, saw octave bass, rock drums |\n| `briefing` | briefings, the hub card | 90 bpm, a tense pad (triangle and pulse12), a ticking hi-hat |\n| `harbor` | Stage 1 | 150 bpm, festival latin-rock: tresillo bass, square lead, clave-like drums; layers `drums` and `lead` |\n| `storm` | Stage 2 | 160 bpm, driving minor, galloping bass, noise \"thunder\" hits |\n| `tidewall` | Stage 3 | 155 bpm, heroic, modulating up a step at 3-3 |\n| `boss` | 1-B, 2-B, mini-bosses | 170 bpm, aggressive |\n| `kingtide` | the final boss | 165 bpm, epic; tempo up for the FINAL SHOT |\n| `range` | Training | light funk |\n| `results` / `clear` (sting) / `continue` / `gameover` / `ending` (a slow ballad version of `theme`) | | |\n\n**SFX**:\n- the 4 weapons; empty click; reload; switching;\n- cover in and out (a cloth whoosh, a thud);\n- whizz; ricochet; impacts on metal, wood, concrete, water and glass; enemy hit, headshot \"ding\" and death barks;\n- the threat tick and chirp; the TIME tick, TIME EXTEND, TIDE'S IN;\n- ammo pickup, 1UP, NEW WEAPON;\n- explosions (small and big), barrel and tank fire;\n- grenade bounce; rocket whoosh; harpoon twang; torpedo hiss; missile; flare pop;\n- turret spin-up; the minigun; the Scylla's stomp and servo; rotor; jet ski; boat engine;\n- glass break, lantern burn, wood break;\n- UI: move, confirm, back, a rank stamp, count-up ticks.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Build order and milestones\nEvery milestone ends with: its tests green in `node tests/run.mjs`, the bundle building, and `tools/check.mjs` free of\nerrors.\n\n| # | Milestone | Done when (acceptance) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0** | **Setup.** The dev folder, the engine copy, the tools, `hub/` files, `package.json`, `build.mjs`, `run.mjs`, a title text in the bundle | The bundle opens from `file://` with no errors; the build test passes (meta order, session client byte-identical, hub tags, no external URLs); the runner prints its count line |\n| **M1** | **Renderer spike** (the biggest risk; do it first). math3d, the texture bank, a textured and lit box room with a floor, water and sky, an `E.shapeMesh` crate, **a Humanoid billboard half-hidden behind the crate**, a corridor that tests near clipping, a muzzle-flash light | Unit tests for projection round trips, near clipping (no NaN, 0–2 triangles), the z-test, and billboard compositing on synthetic pixels; 3 screenshots (actor at 6, 12 and 24 m) look right |\n| **M2** | **The core loop** in a grey-box version of 1-1. Sim and commands, RailCam slots and cover, aim (mouse, pad, keys), the handgun and reload, `deckhand` with peeks, the ThreatDirector and the crisis flash, lives, TIME, clear → WAIT → travel → the next scene, the HUD basics, basic SFX | Tests: the cover timings and `exposed`; no firing in cover; fire in cover switches weapons; reload; rays hit the head and torso and are blocked by cover; threats hit exposed players and are blocked in cover; pop-out protection; TIME counts only in ACTION; time-up; the scene flow |\n| **M3** | **Combat roster.** All 4 weapons, every archetype with its entries, reactions and deaths, projectiles, breakables, barrels, pickups, civilians, allies; **engine patch 1** (the long guns) | One scripted test per archetype and per object; filmstrips of the pop-up, the deaths and the rusher's slash |\n| **M3.5** | **Net spike.** Host and replica with a FakeHub in Node on the grey-box scene; a minimal session build | The net suite passes at 2 and 4 players with latency, jitter and loss; the harness passes `players=2` and `scenario=server` |\n| **M4** | **Stage 1 complete**: the geometry and look, scenes 1-1…1-4, Bulldog, the Stingray/Barracuda boss, cutscenes and briefings, **the voice synth**, music and SFX, results, continue, game over and initials | The content validators pass; the `fair` bot clears Stage 1 on Normal; cutscenes run headless to the end, and skipping works; screenshots of every scene |\n| **M5** | **Stage 2 complete**: rain and lightning, the funicular, The Gull, shields, rushers, the hostage, Hammerhead with degrading cover | As M4, for Stage 2 |\n| **M6** | **Stage 3 complete**: drones, rockets, the GL, the sluice locks, Seawolf, the turbines, the lift, Scylla, Krake, the FINAL SHOT, the ending and the credits | As M4; the `--playthrough` cheat run reaches the ending and writes records |\n| **M7** | **Front end and attract**: the title flyover, menus, difficulty, select, briefing, Training, records, about, how-to, settings items, device-aware prompts, glyph patch 2, wheel patch 3, the touch-only notice, the attract cycle | UI flow tests; attract tests (10 s idle → demo, input → title, the playlist cycles, the watchdog); prompt tests per device and glyph family |\n| **M8** | **Dev mode**: the panel, every slider, toggle and action, the overlays, the free camera, reset | Each slider changes `tune`; reset restores `TUNE` exactly; each action works (tested) |\n| **M9** | **Local co-op**: join, split screen, per-player HUD, continues | Co-op tests: two cameras, independent cover and hits, pickups to the killer, continues per player |\n| **M10** | **Full AI Hub integration**: our own card, stats and awards, every scenario | All 4 harness scenarios pass (`__hubCheck.pass`); the game still runs outside a session |\n| **M11** | **Polish and balance**: juice, the audio mix, the `fair` bot's balance (`tests/balance.json`), screenshot reviews at 16:9, 4:3 and 21:9, `About` data, `exit-interview.json`, the final bundle | The §9 checklist is all ticked; `--all` is green |\n\n**Cut order, if time runs short.** Cut whole scenes, never mechanics. The validators must pass after each cut.\n1. 3-4 Tower Lift: the Seawolf's finale moves into the end of 3-2.\n2. 2-2 Net Lofts: the shield and the rappellers move into 2-1 and 2-4.\n3. 1-3 Container Yard: the Bulldog moves into 1-2's street exit.\n4. The intel bottles.\n5. The allies' appearances in single player.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Risks and how to de-risk them\n| Risk | Why it's risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **The software renderer** (correctness, look, speed) | It is the largest piece of new code, and everything depends on it | M1 comes first, with unit tests for projection, clipping, depth and compositing, and screenshots. Use typed arrays and no allocations in inner loops; cull by chunk and per object; tessellate big faces; give the dev perf overlay ms per pass. Fallbacks: affine spans of 16 px; a lower internal resolution for the 3D pass only |\n| **Rig billboards in perspective** (scale, angle, ground contact, night light) | The engine draws rigs orthographically, from views that can't look up | Bearing-based yaw per actor; pitch clamped to 3° or more; a chest-depth bias; blob shadows; light per actor with a floor of 0.45. Filmstrips at 3 distances and bearings in M1 and M3 |\n| **Hit fidelity** (what you see vs what you hit) | Players feel every miss | Hit volumes from the rig's joints every step; the dev \"show hit volumes\" overlay; tests that aim at `rig.J.head` and expect HEADSHOT |\n| **Pad aiming feel** | A light gun on a stick feels slow | The response curve, acceleration and aim assist (friction and magnetism), all as sliders; the `fair` bot's time-to-target as a metric; early hands-on tests in M2 |\n| **Threat fairness** | Unreadable damage kills the genre | Telegraphs read by shape, sound and arrow; `maxThreats`, `minGap`, pop-out protection; tests that inject overlapping threats |\n| **Content volume** (3 stages) | Big, and easy to leave half-done | Prefabs, data scenes, validators, the free camera with Copy pose; finish Stage 1 completely before starting Stage 2; the cut order in §6 |\n| **Netcode and hub compliance** | Latency and loss, the server and host-leave scenarios | The M3.5 spike; FakeHub tests in Node (rates, sizes, standings, leave, time-up); the real harness in Chromium; the host authoritative and the replica cosmetic |\n| **Engine patches regressing the engine** | Shared code | Small, documented patches (`PATCHES.md`), each with a test; `node kits/test.mjs brawler` and `shooter` from the handoff copy still pass |\n| **The single-file bundle** | Script order, the session client first, size | The build test parses the output; `check.mjs` opens it from `file://` |\n| **The attract bot getting stuck** | An endless loop on a kiosk | Cheats on, the watchdog, a highlight timeout, tests over the whole playlist |\n| **Voice synth timing and CPU** | Many nodes | Schedule ahead in the audio clock; at most 2 dialog voices and 4 barks; a headless no-op path; the dev Voice test |\n| **Determinism drift** | Breaks the tests, the replays and the net rewind | Seeded streams per system; a test greps the sim files for `Math.random`; a test that the same seed and commands give the same `sim.hash()` |\n| **`/tmp` full** | Browsers fail with misleading errors | `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for every browser tool (§0.3) |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Testing\n\n### 8.1 The one command\n`node tests/run.mjs [suite …] [--playthrough] [--browser] [--hub] [--all]`\n- It loads `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and `build/game.js` into a fresh `vm` context for each suite (the pattern of the\n  handoff's `game/test.mjs`), headless, where `draw` is skipped. It rebuilds `build/game.js` first if any `src/` file\n  is newer.\n- Each suite is `export default async t => { … }`, using:\n  - `t.check(name, ok, detail)`;\n  - `t.load({ seed, mode })` → `{ E, game, debug }`;\n  - `t.step(seconds)`, which wraps `game.advance`;\n  - helpers `aimAt(world point, player)`, `fire`, `cover`.\n- **The output is only `FAIL suite › check: detail` lines, then one line, `N passed, M failed (T s)`.** The exit code\n  is 1 on any failure.\n- `game.debug`:\n  - `snapshot()`: scene, phase, stage, scene id, timer, players, enemies, threats, boss, errors;\n  - `jump`, `cheat`, `bot(on, style)`, `aimAt`, `fire`, `cover`;\n  - `sim` and `tune`.\n- Every suite ends by checking that `game.errors` is empty.\n\n### 8.2 Suites (what each part is tested by)\n| Suite | Checks |\n|---|---|\n| `build` | `<meta charset>` comes first, then the session client (sha256 equal to `hub/session.js`), then the hub tags (goal ≤ 60 characters, howto ≤ 80); the engine before the game; no `http(s)://` fetches; `exit-interview.json` parses and has every key |\n| `math3d` | project and unproject round trips; aim → ray → aim; ray vs box, sphere and capsule; the yaw and pitch conventions (yaw 0 looks east, right is +y) |\n| `raster` | near-plane clipping cases; the depth test (a near quad hides a far one in a 16×16 buffer); band dithering stays in range; billboard compositing with depth; fog quantization |\n| `materials` | every material builds 5 distinct bands; the lid variants; the canvas textures headless-safe |\n| `geometry` | `E.shapeMesh` import; prefabs give colliders; `TC.H.rig` is 24–30 u |\n| `content` | every validator in §4.10, over every stage |\n| `input` | `label()` per device and glyph family (PlayStation by default, Xbox via the setting); wheel codes; pointer → aim exact; pad curve, acceleration and assist (friction near a target, none on civilians) |\n| `cover` | blend timings; `exposed`; hold vs toggle; reload in cover; fire in cover switches weapons |\n| `weapons` | fire rates; magazine and pools; pellets; GL splash and falloff; the bloom; switch times; ammo carried over; auto-switch when empty |\n| `player` | lives; i-frames; continue (score reset, the mark); extra lives at the thresholds; the life ring |\n| `timer` | counts only in ACTION and boss; TIME EXTEND; TIDE'S IN; the refill; the clear bonus |\n| `scoring` | points by event; the chain growing, capping and resetting; the ranks |\n| `enemies` | one scripted scenario per archetype: its entry, peek and fire plan, death by every style, the quartermaster's drop and flight, shield immunity and knock-aside, the rusher's slash vs cover, the sniper's laser, drones, jet skis, the captor and hostage |\n| `threats` | `maxThreats`, `minGap`, pop-out protection, always-threat kinds, the ring timing, misses never damaging |\n| `projectiles` | each kind shootable; grenade, rocket and missile blocked by cover; the torpedo not blocked; explosions damaging enemies only |\n| `objects` | barrel chains; breakables removing colliders; the civilian penalty; allies passing shots through; bottles going to INTEL |\n| `bosses` | each boss: phases advance on scripted damage (`debug.fire` at its parts), cover degradation and the swap, the topple and cockpit, the FINAL SHOT hit and miss paths, defeat → outro |\n| `story` | every cutscene runs headless to its end; skipping lands on the same end state; every speaker and voice exists; voice durations are positive |\n| `audio` | every song parses (each track has a whole number of steps); every SFX name exists; layers by phase |\n| `ui` | title → menu → ARCADE → difficulty → briefing → play → pause → Dev mode → reset → quit to title; results → initials → records; About pages are complete with no empty fields; the touch-only notice (stubbed `matchMedia`) |\n| `dev` | each slider changes its `tune` path; reset restores `TUNE` deep-equal; each action works |\n| `attract` | 10 s idle → demo; any input → title (consumed); the playlist cycles; the watchdog advances |\n| `coop` | P2 joins; 2 viewports; independent cameras and cover; separate hits and continues; pickups to the killer |\n| `net` | FakeHub (injectable `hub` object): 1, 2 and 4 players; latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5%; server mode; host leave; time-up → `finish` with valid standings and scores; ≤ 20 messages a second per copy; every `s` ≤ 1,200 bytes; kills credited to the right player; replicas converge |\n| `determinism` | the same seed and commands give the same `sim.hash()` after 60 s; no `Math.random` in sim files; no hardcoded key names in prompts |\n| `--playthrough` | the `fair` bot clears Stages 1, 2 and 3 on Normal without a continue (and records the time per scene to `tests/balance.json`, which the content suite reads); the `showoff` cheat bot plays the whole ARCADE to the credits and the initials; the Training range completes |\n| `--browser` | `tools/check.mjs` on the bundle at 1920×1080, 1280×720, 2560×1080 and 1024×768: no errors, the canvas filled, screenshots of the title, 1-1, a boss and split screen |\n| `--hub` | `tools/hubcheck.mjs` copies the bundle and the harness files into `hubtest/`, serves it on `127.0.0.1:0`, confirms the page is ours, then runs `harness.html?game=…&players=2&auto=1`, `…&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with `&scenario=host-leave`, and `…&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. It waits for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, reads `window.__hubCheck.pass`, and prints only the failed checks. It kills its server by PID |\n\n### 8.3 What only eyes can check (screenshots and filmstrips)\n- The M1 renderer spike.\n- One screenshot per scene; every boss in each phase.\n- The HUD at 16:9, 4:3 and 21:9; split screen; the title and menus; the attract overlay; the touch-only notice.\n- Filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`): the cover duck, an enemy pop-up, each death style, the rusher's slash,\n  Hammerhead's sweep, the Scylla's gait and topple, every engine weapon pose.\n\nRerun only after changing what they show.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Done checklist (TASK.md → where it's covered)\n- [ ] **Title** picked by RNG from 50 riffs: Tide Crisis 3 (the top of this plan).\n- [ ] **Genre and perspective** chosen: an on-rails light-gun shooter with cover, in first person (§1).\n- [ ] **The single HTML** and the dev folder with the exact names; plays from `file://` (§0.1, §3.2).\n- [ ] **Built on the handoff engine**; the changes logged in `engine/PATCHES.md` (§3.6).\n- [ ] **Art** in the engine's native style with new assets (§4.1, §5.10); **animation** on the engine's rigs with new\n      moves (§5.11).\n- [ ] **Audio** all in code: music, SFX and gibberish voices (§4.12, §5.12).\n- [ ] **Online**: AI Hub shared-world co-op, all 4 harness scenarios pass (§4.19); **multiplayer on its own**: local\n      split-screen co-op (§4.18).\n- [ ] **Every mechanic** shown in the demo:\n  - cover and reload; 4 weapons and switching; quartermaster ammo; the crisis flash;\n  - Red Tide; grenades, rockets, torpedoes, missiles and flares shot down;\n  - shields, rushers, snipers, drones, jet skis, vehicles, hostages, civilians;\n  - breakables and barrels; life rings and intel; TIME, TIME EXTEND and TIDE'S IN;\n  - chain, ranks, continues, initials;\n  - moving scenes; 3 bosses, 3 mini-bosses and the FINAL SHOT;\n  - Training (§5).\n- [ ] **Dev mode** from the pause menu: live sliders, toggles, actions, reset to defaults (§4.16).\n- [ ] **Attract mode** after 10 s idle on the title or menu, a looping AI demo, any input exits (§4.17).\n- [ ] **10-foot, controller-first UI**:\n  - DualSense mapping; native keyboard and mouse (the mouse aims and its hover moves the focus);\n  - prompts follow the last device; PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option;\n  - no dense screens (§4.3, §4.13–4.15).\n- [ ] **Touch-only**: \"Controller or keyboard required\" with the settings button, and the attract mode runs (§4.14).\n- [ ] **Narrative tone** in the source's B-movie style, with every beat scripted (§5.2, §5.9).\n- [ ] **Tests**: one command printing only failures and a count; a scripted playthrough of the whole game; headless\n      `game.advance`/`game.debug` (§8).\n- [ ] **No TODOs, placeholders or stubs.** A last check:\n      `grep -rniE \"todo|fixme|placeholder|lorem|stub\" src/` returns nothing.\n- [ ] **About/Credits screen** with Source Information, Testing Feedback (4), Engine Feedback (6) and Prompt Feedback\n      (4) (§4.14).\n- [ ] **`exit-interview.json`** in the exact shape, every value filled (\"unknown\" where unconfirmed), parsed by a test.\n      Suggested `aiHub` block:\n      `{ \"name\": \"Tide Crisis 3\", \"tagline\": \"Duck. Pop. Shoot. Beat the tide.\", \"description\": \"An original arcade light-gun rail shooter in PS1-style pixel 3D: duck behind cover, switch between four weapons and race each area's clock to retake an island's tidal barrier before the dawn king tide. Play solo, couch co-op or AI Hub co-op for up to four.\", \"type\": \"Game\", \"genre\": \"Shooter\", \"source\": \"Time Crisis 3\", \"series\": \"Time Crisis\", \"players\": \"1–4\", \"controls\": \"Mouse or stick aims · left click/R2 fires · hold right click/L2 for cover and reload · wheel/R1 switches weapons\", \"tags\": [\"first-person\", \"arcade\", \"co-op\", \"boss fights\", \"pixel art\", \"retro\"] }`\n- [ ] **The final chat reply** repeats Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback.\n","numLines":392,"startLine":1280,"totalLines":1671}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01SCJekaiRDoPVjUdsp2j5wh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
