{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LWGxqKj48DCQqhvpD747jR","type":"tool_result","content":"8:billboards (rigs drawn at the size their distance gives, sprites, your own drawing) far to near.\n15:- In draw: m7.rig(rig, x, y, z), m7.sprite(spr or E.anim, x, y, z, { scale, flip, t }), m7.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing,\n17:  far to near, as an overlay (in a split screen, in r.viewport: give each player's cam).\n21:  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n32:Rules: m7.draw covers its viewport (draw nothing under it you need to see); move the camera in update, not draw; a\n44:const trig = a => { let c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a); if (Math.abs(c) < 1e-12) c = 0; if (Math.abs(s) < 1e-12) s = 0; return [c, s]; };\n58:    const a = o.angle !== undefined ? o.angle : b.angle || 0, back = o.back === undefined ? 56 : o.back, [c, s] = trig(a);\n65:    const P = this._P, W = rect.W, H = rect.H, pd = cam.pitch === undefined ? 12 : cam.pitch, pitch = pd * Math.PI / 180, [fx, fy] = trig(cam.angle || 0);\n90:  /** gather a rig, drawn by the engine at the size its distance gives, from the camera's side (it faces rig.facing) */\n91:  rig(rig, x, y, z = 0) { return this.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => rig.draw(g, Math.round(sx), Math.round(sy), this.view(k))); }\n109:  /** the engine view a rig is drawn with at k pixels per unit, seen from the camera's heading (sixteenths, reused) */\n112:    let v = this._views.get(key); if (!v) { if (this._views.size > 400) this._views.clear(); v = new E.View('mode7', 'Mode 7', yaw, this._pd, q, 1); this._views.set(key, v); }\n115:  /** draw the view as an overlay over r's frame (in a split screen, r.viewport's part): sky, floor, fog, then the\n116:   *  billboards far to near (gathered with add, rig, sprite; they are used up) */\n118:    const vp = r.viewport || { x: 0, y: 0, w: r.bw, h: r.bh }, items = this.items.splice(0), sc = r.game.screen, whole = !r.viewport;\n119:    r.overlay(g => {\n122:      // drawn on a canvas of the viewport's size (moved so screen points land on it), then onto the frame\n150:    const cv = E.mkCanvas(W, H), g = cv.getContext('2d'), img = g.createImageData(W, H), d = img.data;\n155:    g.putImageData(img, 0, 0); return (this._tex = cv);\n171:      if (!this._px) this._px = new Uint32Array(F.getContext('2d').getImageData(0, 0, TW, TH).data.buffer);\n173:      const B = this._buf && this._buf.width === w && this._buf.height === h ? this._buf : (this._buf = E.mkCanvas(w, h)), bg = B.getContext('2d'), img = bg.createImageData(w, h), out = new Uint32Array(img.data.buffer);\n185:      bg.putImageData(img, 0, 0); g.drawImage(B, vp.x, top);\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183213__xf5fb84/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14efaf47-c831-41be-b2ba-0398106a097f","uuid":"8655448c-6f80-4e6f-bed2-41d446f7b852","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:33:26.393Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"8:billboards (rigs drawn at the size their distance gives, sprites, your own drawing) far to near.\n15:- In draw: m7.rig(rig, x, y, z), m7.sprite(spr or E.anim, x, y, z, { scale, flip, t }), m7.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing,\n17:  far to near, as an overlay (in a split screen, in r.viewport: give each player's cam).\n21:  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n32:Rules: m7.draw covers its viewport (draw nothing under it you need to see); move the camera in update, not draw; a\n44:const trig = a => { let c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a); if (Math.abs(c) < 1e-12) c = 0; if (Math.abs(s) < 1e-12) s = 0; return [c, s]; };\n58:    const a = o.angle !== undefined ? o.angle : b.angle || 0, back = o.back === undefined ? 56 : o.back, [c, s] = trig(a);\n65:    const P = this._P, W = rect.W, H = rect.H, pd = cam.pitch === undefined ? 12 : cam.pitch, pitch = pd * Math.PI / 180, [fx, fy] = trig(cam.angle || 0);\n90:  /** gather a rig, drawn by the engine at the size its distance give