{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XmzoRUxiebimCRf7Cp1BKt","type":"tool_result","content":"896:  codeLabel(code) {\n  codeLabel(code) {\n    if (!code) return '';\n    const L = this._layout && this._layout.get && this._layout.get(code);\n    if (/^Key[A-Z]$/.test(code)) return (L || code.slice(3)).toUpperCase();\n    if (/^Digit\\d$/.test(code)) return L || code.slice(5);\n    if (/^Pad\\d+$/.test(code)) return (PAD_GLYPHS[this.padStyle()] || PAD_GLYPHS.xbox)[+code.slice(3)] || code;\n    return CODE_LABELS[code] || (code.startsWith('Numpad') ? 'Num ' + code.slice(6) : code.startsWith('Act:') ? code.slice(4).toUpperCase() : code);\n1010:  tap(a) { if (!this.map[a]) { this._check(a); return; } this._tapCode('Act:' + a); }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14efaf47-c831-41be-b2ba-0398106a097f","uuid":"8553c0dd-88a4-475f-9de3-164530dcccdc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:04.204Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"896:  codeLabel(code) {\n  codeLabel(code) {\n    if (!code) return '';\n    const L = this._layout && this._layout.get && this._layout.get(code);\n    if (/^Key[A-Z]$/.test(code)) return (L || code.slice(3)).toUpperCase();\n    if (/^Digit\\d$/.test(code)) return L || code.slice(5);\n    if (/^Pad\\d+$/.test(code)) return (PAD_GLYPHS[this.padStyle()] || PAD_GLYPHS.xbox)[+code.slice(3)] || code;\n    return CODE_LABELS[code] || (code.startsWith('Numpad') ? 'Num ' + code.slice(6) : code.startsWith('Act:') ? code.slice(4).toUpperCase() : code);\n1010:  tap(a) { if (!this.map[a]) { this._check(a); return; } this._tapCode('Act:' + a); }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1955,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1955,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2hWKbCLipuHyFhGFvx\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5908,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":515877,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":5908},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc\",\"uuid\":\"692cfd5a-4d92-491c-bfdf-cf515a7cbfca\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:35:59.671Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2hW3iMmDLrH6oJ6FTr\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":2321,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011Cgh2hWKbCLipuHyFhGFvx\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01CtbVRyJcz6AS4xrWpeQWX3\",\"name\":\"Read\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1185,\"limit\":110},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":5908,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":515877,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":5908},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc\",\"uuid\":\"3450e700-2d0d-4a7c-8ccb-543519269716\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:36:01.350Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cgh2hW3iMmDLrH6oJ6FTr\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01CtbVRyJcz6AS4xrWpeQWX3\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md\",\"offset\":1185,\"limit\":110}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01CtbVRyJcz6AS4xrWpeQWX3\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"1185\\t\\n1186\\tSongs are written in the engine's step notation (`{ bpm, steps, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, notes, on }] }`), in an\\n1187\\t\\\"alpine noir\\\" style: pulse-wave accordion chords, triangle and saw oompah bass, pulse12 zither arpeggios, sine pads\\n1188\\twith vibrato, brushed noise hats. Every play song has an **explore** layer and a **danger** layer (`on: false`).\\n1189\\t`audio.layer('danger', 1, .5)` brings the danger layer in while enemies are alive within 40 m, and it fades out\\n1190\\t1.5 s after the last one dies.\\n1191\\t\\n1192\\t| Song | Where | Sketch |\\n1193\\t|---|---|---|\\n1194\\t| `title` | title | a slow minor waltz on pulse, then the SKILLER7 motif (a falling minor sixth and a rising seventh) |\\n1195\\t| `room7` | Room 7 | a music box (triangle, high) in 3/4, a ticking clock, distant wind noise |\\n1196\\t| `hotel` | 00A–00B | lounge jazz in D minor: a walking bass (triangle), muted trumpet (square with vibrato), brushes; danger: dissonant stabs |\\n1197\\t| `shaft` | Grau | a lift-bell motif (\\\"ding\\\") as a rhythm; a faster pulse with each phase (`audio.tempo`) |\\n1198\\t| `village` | 01A | an oompah polka in a minor key, half a step flat on purpose; danger: snare rolls |\\n1199\\t| `palais` | 01B | bureaucratic minimal: arpeggiated sines, typewriter-click hats, a cold pad |\\n1200\\t| `band` | the Jolly Four | a polka with four named tracks `tuba`, `accordion`, `trumpet`, `snare`. Each track's notes are that musician's vulnerability windows (§11.8). 112 → 124 → 136 → 148 bpm |\\n1201\\t| `blackrun` | 01C | driving bass and a yodel-like lead with octave jumps; avalanche: tempo up plus a choir pad |\\n1202\\t| `gondola` | 01D | suspended pads, creaking-cable rhythm (filtered noise), a slow heartbeat kick |\\n1203\\t| `archive` | 01E | drones and crystalline bells (sine arps), a heartbeat |\\n1204\\t| `powderking` | Hansi | a cheerful schlager, ironic and distorted; phase 2 drops to a slalom gallop; phase 3 is a lone pad |\\n1205\\t| `echorun` | Echo Run | fast, bright, a countdown sting |\\n1206\\t| jingles | — | `stage` (a target eliminated), `gameover`, `rank` |\\n1207\\t\\n1208\\t### 10.2 Sound effects (`70-audio.js`; `audio.define(name, voice)` and lists of voices)\\n1209\\t\\n1210\\t- **Weapons:** fire and reload for all seven; dry fire; overheat; scope in and out.\\n1211\\t- **Combat:** Scan (a sonar ping and an expanding whoosh); crit (a glass crack, a choir chord); body kill (a slush\\n1212\\t  splat); explosion (a wet pop and a low thump); shield TINK; the giggle-up rattle; snowball whoosh and hit.\\n1213\\t- **Movement:** footsteps by surface (snow crunch, marble click, wood creak, ice tick); ski swoosh (filtered noise\\n1214\\t  following speed); carve hiss; hockey-stop spray; jump and landing; lift hum and clacks; gondola creak; avalanche rumble\\n1215\\t  (low noise with an LFO).\\n1216\\t- **World:** church bell (inharmonic partials), service bell, cuckoo call, phone ring (a mechanical bell), Room 7 door\\n1217\\t  (a soft major chord), Echo (a long yodel echo), Flash (a pop and whine), Flare (a fizz), Make It Rain (coins), Control\\n1218\\t  Charge (a deep boom), wax hiss, Edelweiss slot (a chime per pass), ice lock steam.\\n1219\\t- **UI:** focus tick, confirm, back, the switch flurry swish, the ring opening, card sting, the THAW splash, RED +n\\n1220\\t  blips.\\n1221\\t- **Ambience:** wind beds (filtered noise in two bands, slow gusts; the Föhn is a warm, low, whistling gust); hotel room\\n1222\\t  tone; the village crowd murmur (gibberish voices at low level, §10.4); the archive's dripping.\\n1223\\t\\n1224\\t### 10.3 Laughter (`72-laugh.js`)\\n1225\\t\\n1226\\t- One synth voice per laugh: a sawtooth or pulse source at the laugh's pitch → two band-pass formant filters for \\\"ha\\\"\\n1227\\t  (F1 750 Hz, F2 1200 Hz) → a gain envelope, plus a breath noise burst before each syllable.\\n1228\\t- **Styles:**\\n1229\\t  - giggle: 6–10 syllables, 90 ms each, high, rising;\\n1230\\t  - cackle: 4–6, harsh, a pulse source, pitch falling;\\n1231\\t  - chuckle: 3–4, low, soft;\\n1232\\t  - wheeze: mostly noise.\\n1233\\t  Each Whiteout has a seeded style and pitch (±3 semitones).\\n1234\\t- **Positional:** a `StereoPannerNode` from the camera-relative angle, gain from distance (60 m silent), and a lowpass\\n1235\\t  at 900 Hz when the LevelGrid line of sight is blocked. At most 8 laughs at once (the nearest).\\n1236\\t- It runs on `game.audio.ctx` into our own buses: voice and laugh gains = `sfxVolume × voices × (muted ? 0 : 1)`,\\n1237\\t  updated each frame. Headless, there is no AudioContext and it does nothing.\\n1238\\t\\n1239\\t### 10.4 Voices: Animalese-style gibberish (`71-voice.js`, `content/voices.js`)\\n1240\\t\\n1241\\t- **Per letter, synced to the dialog's typing:** each step, compare `talk.shown` with the last count. For each newly\\n1242\\t  typed letter (every second one, skipping spaces and punctuation), play a syllable of 55–80 ms. Vowels set the formants\\n1243\\t  (a 800/1200, e 400/2300, i 300/2700, o 450/800, u 325/700 Hz); a consonant before a vowel adds a 12 ms noise burst\\n1244\\t  (s, z, f: high-passed; t, k, p: a click). Commas pause 120 ms, full stops 250 ms. A \\\"?\\\" rises the last 3 syllables by\\n1245\\t  3 semitones; \\\"!\\\" adds gain and a +2 semitone accent. The pitch drifts down over a sentence.\\n1246\\t- **Speakers** (base pitch Hz, range in semitones, rate, source, extras):\\n1247\\t\\n1248\\t| Speaker | Pitch | Range | Rate | Source | Extras |\\n1249\\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n1250\\t| Oma Holle | 420 | ±5 | slow | triangle | a quavering 6 Hz vibrato, quiet |\\n1251\\t| Sister Rosalind | 260 | ±2 | clipped | pulse | dry |\\n1252\\t| The Concierge | 120 | ±1 | slow | saw | telephone band (bandpass 300–3400 Hz), crackle |\\n1253\\t| Mister Föhn | 160 | ±4 | lilting | sine + breath noise | a warm glide between syllables |\\n1254\\t| Pim | 520 | ±3 | quick | triangle | an echo (feedback delay 180 ms) |\\n1255\\t| Murmel | 200 | ±2 | slow | saw | muffled (lowpass 600 Hz), a ... pause every 3 syllables |\\n1256\\t| Ansel | 110 | ±1 | slow | saw | — |\\n1257\\t| Dagny | 330 | ±3 | fast | pulse | — |\\n1258\\t| Ignaz | 140 | ±2 | slow | saw | a slight tremolo |\\n1259\\t| Rurik | 95 | ±2 | medium | saw | a gravelly noise layer |\\n1260\\t| Kasimir | 180 | ±7 | bouncy | pulse | yodel octave flips on stressed syllables |\\n1261\\t| Mireille | 300 | ±4 | medium | triangle | breathy |\\n1262\\t| Brigid | 240 | ±2 | medium | pulse | flat and dry |\\n1263\\t| Grau | 150 | ±1 | medium | square | a \\\"ding\\\" on every 5th syllable |\\n1264\\t| Hansi | 210 | ±5 | hearty | pulse | a cheerful lilt |\\n1265\\t| Whiteouts | 300–500 | ±6 | random | — | laughter fragments inside words |\\n1266\\t\\n1267\\t- Volume comes from the `voices` setting. The ring and barks use the same voices (short phrases).\\n1268\\t\\n1269\\t**Tests (headless):** the voice module is a no-op without an AudioContext; a syllable schedule from text is\\n1270\\tdeterministic (the same text gives the same list); the dialog hookup counts letters correctly across pages.\\n1271\\t\\n1272\\t---\\n1273\\t\\n1274\\t## 11. Content\\n1275\\t\\n1276\\t### 11.1 World and premise\\n1277\\t\\n1278\\t- **The Free Canton of Piz Nada**, population \\\"discreet\\\": a neutral micro-state of one mountain, one village\\n1279\\t  (**Oberglück**), the **Grand Hotel Nada**, a conference palace (the **Palais des Neiges**), ski runs, the\\n1280\\t  **Himmelsbahn** gondola, and under the summit glacier the **Glacier Archive**, where the Canton's banks keep the\\n1281\\t  deposits of every nation, some of them people. It has snowed for a hundred years.\\n1282\\t- **The Thaw Accord:** the **Coastal Federation** and the **Steppe Directorate** will sign it at the summit at\\n1283\\t  midnight to end forty years of frozen war. Article Nine makes the Canton open the Archive.\\n1284\\t- **Mister Föhn**, the warm wind, wants everything to melt: \\\"Everything comes out in the thaw.\\\" People he touches laugh\\n1285\\t  until they are invisible: the **Whiteouts**. His agents are the **Warm Front**.\\n1286\\t- **Oma Holle**, 104, keeps the mountain frozen by shaking her featherbed. In 1926 a chairlift of eight young skiers\\n1287\\t  was caught by an avalanche; she was the only one found alive. Her seven personas have the faces and skills of the\\n1288\\t  seven who weren't. (The demo hints at this and never states it.)\\n1289\\t- **The Department of Discretion**, through **the Concierge**, sends her \\\"guests\\\" to check out. Is she the hero?\\n1290\\t  Who pays the Department? The demo ends on that question.\\n1291\\t\\n1292\\t### 11.2 Writing style guide (Killer7's register, our world)\\n1293\\t\\n1294\\t- **Short, flat sentences**, mostly under 12 words. People answer the question underneath the one asked, or another\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc\",\"uuid\":\"1801415b-8a11-4c20-9c70-1a3751477fff\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T01:36:01.356Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/work/PLAN.md\",\"content\":\"\\nSongs are written in the engine's step notation (`{ bpm, steps, tracks: [{ name, wave, vol, notes, on }] }`), in an\\n\\\"alpine noir\\\" style: pulse-wave accordion chords, triangle and saw oompah bass, pulse12 zither arpeggios, sine pads\\nwith vibrato, brushed noise hats. Every play song has an **explore** layer and a **danger** layer (`on: false`).\\n`audio.layer('danger', 1, .5)` brings the danger layer in while enemies are alive within 40 m, and it fades out\\n1.5 s after the last one dies.\\n\\n| Song | Where | Sketch |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `title` | title | a slow minor waltz on pulse, then the SKILLER7 motif (a falling minor sixth and a rising seventh) |\\n| `room7` | Room 7 | a music box (triangle, high) in 3/4, a ticking clock, distant wind noise |\\n| `hotel` | 00A–00B | lounge jazz in D minor: a walking bass (triangle), muted trumpet (square with vibrato), brushes; danger: dissonant stabs |\\n| `shaft` | Grau | a lift-bell motif (\\\"ding\\\") as a rhythm; a faster pulse with each phase (`audio.tempo`) |\\n| `village` | 01A | an oompah polka in a minor key, half a step flat on purpose; danger: snare rolls |\\n| `palais` | 01B | bureaucratic minimal: arpeggiated sines, typewriter-click hats, a cold pad |\\n| `band` | the Jolly Four | a polka with four named tracks `tuba`, `accordion`, `trumpet`, `snare`. Each track's notes are that musician's vulnerability windows (§11.8). 112 → 124 → 136 → 148 bpm |\\n| `blackrun` | 01C | driving bass and a yodel-like lead with octave jumps; avalanche: tempo up plus a choir pad |\\n| `gondola` | 01D | suspended pads, creaking-cable rhythm (filtered noise), a slow heartbeat kick |\\n| `archive` | 01E | drones and crystalline bells (sine arps), a heartbeat |\\n| `powderking` | Hansi | a cheerful schlager, ironic and distorted; phase 2 drops to a slalom gallop; phase 3 is a lone pad |\\n| `echorun` | Echo Run | fast, bright, a countdown sting |\\n| jingles | — | `stage` (a target eliminated), `gameover`, `rank` |\\n\\n### 10.2 Sound effects (`70-audio.js`; `audio.define(name, voice)` and lists of voices)\\n\\n- **Weapons:** fire and reload for all seven; dry fire; overheat; scope in and out.\\n- **Combat:** Scan (a sonar ping and an expanding whoosh); crit (a glass crack, a choir chord); body kill (a slush\\n  splat); explosion (a wet pop and a low thump); shield TINK; the giggle-up rattle; snowball whoosh and hit.\\n- **Movement:** footsteps by surface (snow crunch, marble click, wood creak, ice tick); ski swoosh (filtered noise\\n  following speed); carve hiss; hockey-stop spray; jump and landing; lift hum and clacks; gondola creak; avalanche rumble\\n  (low noise with an LFO).\\n- **World:** church bell (inharmonic partials), service bell, cuckoo call, phone ring (a mechanical bell), Room 7 door\\n  (a soft major chord), Echo (a long yodel echo), Flash (a pop and whine), Flare (a fizz), Make It Rain (coins), Control\\n  Charge (a deep boom), wax hiss, Edelweiss slot (a chime per pass), ice lock steam.\\n- **UI:** focus tick, confirm, back, the switch flurry swish, the ring opening, card sting, the THAW splash, RED +n\\n  blips.\\n- **Ambience:** wind beds (filtered noise in two bands, slow gusts; the Föhn is a warm, low, whistling gust); hotel room\\n  tone; the village crowd murmur (gibberish voices at low level, §10.4); the archive's dripping.\\n\\n### 10.3 Laughter (`72-laugh.js`)\\n\\n- One synth voice per laugh: a sawtooth or pulse source at the laugh's pitch → two band-pass formant filters for \\\"ha\\\"\\n  (F1 750 Hz, F2 1200 Hz) → a gain envelope, plus a breath noise burst before each syllable.\\n- **Styles:**\\n  - giggle: 6–10 syllables, 90 ms each, high, rising;\\n  - cackle: 4–6, harsh, a pulse source, pitch falling;\\n  - chuckle: 3–4, low, soft;\\n  - wheeze: mostly noise.\\n  Each Whiteout has a seeded style and pitch (±3 semitones).\\n- **Positional:** a `StereoPannerNode` from the camera-relative angle, gain from distance (60 m silent), and a lowpass\\n  at 900 Hz when the LevelGrid line of sight is blocked. At most 8 laughs at once (the nearest).\\n- It runs on `game.audio.ctx` into our own buses: voice and laugh gains = `sfxVolume × voices × (muted ? 0 : 1)`,\\n  updated each frame. Headless, there is no AudioContext and it does nothing.\\n\\n### 10.4 Voices: Animalese-style gibberish (`71-voice.js`, `content/voices.js`)\\n\\n- **Per letter, synced to the dialog's typing:** each step, compare `talk.shown` with the last count. For each newly\\n  typed letter (every second one, skipping spaces and punctuation), play a syllable of 55–80 ms. Vowels set the formants\\n  (a 800/1200, e 400/2300, i 300/2700, o 450/800, u 325/700 Hz); a consonant before a vowel adds a 12 ms noise burst\\n  (s, z, f: high-passed; t, k, p: a click). Commas pause 120 ms, full stops 250 ms. A \\\"?\\\" rises the last 3 syllables by\\n  3 semitones; \\\"!\\\" adds gain and a +2 semitone accent. The pitch drifts down over a sentence.\\n- **Speakers** (base pitch Hz, range in semitones, rate, source, extras):\\n\\n| Speaker | Pitch | Range | Rate | Source | Extras |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Oma Holle | 420 | ±5 | slow | triangle | a quavering 6 Hz vibrato, quiet |\\n| Sister Rosalind | 260 | ±2 | clipped | pulse | dry |\\n| The Concierge | 120 | ±1 | slow | saw | telephone band (bandpass 300–3400 Hz), crackle |\\n| Mister Föhn | 160 | ±4 | lilting | sine + breath noise | a warm glide between syllables |\\n| Pim | 520 | ±3 | quick | triangle | an echo (feedback delay 180 ms) |\\n| Murmel | 200 | ±2 | slow | saw | muffled (lowpass 600 Hz), a ... pause every 3 syllables |\\n| Ansel | 110 | ±1 | slow | saw | — |\\n| Dagny | 330 | ±3 | fast | pulse | — |\\n| Ignaz | 140 | ±2 | slow | saw | a slight tremolo |\\n| Rurik | 95 | ±2 | medium | saw | a gravelly noise layer |\\n| Kasimir | 180 | ±7 | bouncy | pulse | yodel octave flips on stressed syllables |\\n| Mireille | 300 | ±4 | medium | triangle | breathy |\\n| Brigid | 240 | ±2 | medium | pulse | flat and dry |\\n| Grau | 150 | ±1 | medium | square | a \\\"ding\\\" on every 5th syllable |\\n| Hansi | 210 | ±5 | hearty | pulse | a cheerful lilt |\\n| Whiteouts | 300–500 | ±6 | random | — | laughter fragments inside words |\\n\\n- Volume comes from the `voices` setting. The ring and barks use the same voices (short phrases).\\n\\n**Tests (headless):** the voice module is a no-op without an AudioContext; a syllable schedule from text is\\ndeterministic (the same text gives the same list); the dialog hookup counts letters correctly across pages.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. Content\\n\\n### 11.1 World and premise\\n\\n- **The Free Canton of Piz Nada**, population \\\"discreet\\\": a neutral micro-state of one mountain, one village\\n  (**Oberglück**), the **Grand Hotel Nada**, a conference palace (the **Palais des Neiges**), ski runs, the\\n  **Himmelsbahn** gondola, and under the summit glacier the **Glacier Archive**, where the Canton's banks keep the\\n  deposits of every nation, some of them people. It has snowed for a hundred years.\\n- **The Thaw Accord:** the **Coastal Federation** and the **Steppe Directorate** will sign it at the summit at\\n  midnight to end forty years of frozen war. Article Nine makes the Canton open the Archive.\\n- **Mister Föhn**, the warm wind, wants everything to melt: \\\"Everything comes out in the thaw.\\\" People he touches laugh\\n  until they are invisible: the **Whiteouts**. His agents are the **Warm Front**.\\n- **Oma Holle**, 104, keeps the mountain frozen by shaking her featherbed. In 1926 a chairlift of eight young skiers\\n  was caught by an avalanche; she was the only one found alive. Her seven personas have the faces and skills of the\\n  seven who weren't. (The demo hints at this and never states it.)\\n- **The Department of Discretion**, through **the Concierge**, sends her \\\"guests\\\" to check out. Is she the hero?\\n  Who pays the Department? The demo ends on that question.\\n\\n### 11.2 Writing style guide (Killer7's register, our world)\\n\\n- **Short, flat sentences**, mostly under 12 words. People answer the question underneath the one asked, or another\",\"numLines\":110,\"startLine\":1185,\"totalLines\":2116}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01CtbVRyJcz6AS4xrWpeQWX3\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":50,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":50,\"session_id\":\"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc\",\"uuid\":\"c3ea56b9-bb3c-4b6c-9d72-97468854de1c\"}"]}]}],"moreFiles":1,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/agent.out"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XmzoRUxiebimCRf7Cp1BKt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2iAvK1oX7WK1XuGisT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HPMoevVTwFRFBKCBZpRG11","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='engine/my-3d2dge.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    el.addEventListener('wheel', e => {\n      if (!this._wheelOn) return; e.preventDefault();\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    el.addEventListener('wheel', e => {\n      // Tide Crisis patch: 'WheelUp' / 'WheelDown' are codes an action can be bound to (a step's press per notch)\n      const wc = e.deltaY < 0 ? 'WheelUp' : e.deltaY > 0 ? 'WheelDown' : null;\n      if (wc && !this._wheelOn && Object.keys(this.map).some(k => this.map[k].includes(wc))) { e.preventDefault(); this.lastDevice = 'mouse'; if (!this._wheelAt || this.clock - this._wheelAt > .09) { this._wheelAt = this.clock; this._tapCode(wc); } return; }\n      if (!this._wheelOn) return; e.preventDefault();\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"    return CODE_LABELS[code] || (code.startsWith('Numpad')\"\nb=\"    if (code === 'WheelUp') return 'Wheel up'; if (code === 'WheelDown') return 'Wheel down';\\n    return CODE_LABELS[code] || (code.startsWith('Numpad')\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"  _tapCode\" engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -2; cat >> engine/PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n4. **Mouse-wheel codes.** When the scene's zoom is off and an action is bound to `WheelUp` or `WheelDown`, a wheel\n   notch taps that code for one step (at most one per 90 ms); `codeLabel` names them \"Wheel up\" and \"Wheel down\".\n   The wheel switches weapons.\nEOF","description":"Patch wheel codes into engine input"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1010,"cache_read_input_tokens":175373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1010},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14efaf47-c831-41be-b2ba-0398106a097f","uuid":"40b2c8f9-6fac-4d66-8bb1-d89450db3cc0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:11.673Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2iAgfdxZwHq2xHnnrS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HPMoevVTwFRFBKCBZpRG11":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='engine/my-3d2dge.js'; s=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"    el.addEventListener('wheel', e => {\n      if (!this._wheelOn) return; e.preventDefault();\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"    el.addEventListener('wheel', e => {\n      // Tide Crisis patch: 'WheelUp' / 'WheelDown' are codes an action can be bound to (a step's press per notch)\n      const wc = e.deltaY < 0 ? 'WheelUp' : e.deltaY > 0 ? 'WheelDown' : null;\n      if (wc && !this._wheelOn && Object.keys(this.map).some(k => this.map[k].includes(wc))) { e.preventDefault(); this.lastDevice = 'mouse'; if (!this._wheelAt || this.clock - this._wheelAt > .09) { this._wheelAt = this.clock; this._tapCode(wc); } return; }\n      if (!this._wheelOn) return; e.preventDefault();\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\na=\"    return CODE_LABELS[code] || (code.startsWith('Numpad')\"\nb=\"    if (code === 'WheelUp') return 'Wheel up'; if (code === 'WheelDown') return 'Wheel down';\\n    return CODE_LABELS[code] || (code.startsWith('Numpad')\"\nassert s.count(a)==1; s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"  _tapCode\" engine/my-3d2dge.js | head -2; cat >> engine/PATCHES.md <<'EOF'\n4. **Mouse-wheel codes.** When the scene's zoom is off and an action is bound to `WheelUp` or `WheelDown`, a wheel\n   notch taps that code for one step (at most one per 90 ms); `codeLabel` names them \"Wheel up\" and \"Wheel down\".\n   The wheel switches weapons.\nEOF","description":"Patch wheel codes into engine input"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HPMoevVTwFRFBKCBZpRG11","type":"tool_result","content":"1015:  _tapCode(c) { this.press(c); this._taps.add(c); }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"14efaf47-c831-41be-b2ba-0398106a097f","uuid":"1d6ed811-b9e7-447b-9a89-82a631e308ca","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:12.396Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1015:  _tapCode(c) { this.press(c); this._taps.add(c); }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":124,"oldLines":3,"newStart":124,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":2950,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":250,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"08be40aa-160b-4724-b6de-90878eb26a14\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3150,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"e7026c2c-75f9-4268-ac23-bd1da2d7fc29\"}"," {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3350,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"bdcc56e6-5fb7-4237-bcc0-7a7bd39c95d4\"}","+{\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":3550,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":200,\"session_id\":\"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2\",\"uuid\":\"f135634e-92ec-47a8-9d58-fa5602a977ea\"}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174752__xfb4127/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":1961,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1961,"newLines":5,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"system\",\"subtype\":\"thinking_tokens\",\"estimated_tokens\":400,\"estimated_tokens_delta\":100,\"session_id\":\"4e34a208-b0be-46a3-80b7-32b0075578cc\",\"uuid\":\"efc5f883-078